(1046348, 124280, 25355, '<td valign="top">Image too small</td>', 'Image too small', '2004-12-04 19:16:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046349, 123975, 25355, '<td valign="top">Image too small.</td>', 'Image too small.', '2004-12-04 19:17:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046351, 124893, 25355, '<td valign="top">Would have been better in colour, I think.</td>', 'Would have been better in colour, I think.', '2004-12-04 19:20:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046352, 124196, 25355, '<td valign="top">Not technology at all.</td>', 'Not technology at all.', '2004-12-04 19:20:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046355, 122472, 25355, '<td valign="top">Perhaps a shot of boots being worn and taken midstride would have been better. Anyway, I think boots by themselves are technological, but there''s implied technology in the process of making them. Light on the left is blown out too much, strange object on the right.</td>', 'Perhaps a shot of boots being worn and taken midstride would have been better. Anyway, I think boots by themselves are technological, but there''s implied technology in the process of making them. Light on the left is blown out too much, strange object on the right.', '2004-12-04 19:27:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046357, 124983, 25355, '<td valign="top">You put your finger in it.</td>', 'You put your finger in it.', '2004-12-04 19:28:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046468, 123977, 28758, '<td valign="top">Beautiful colors</td>', 'Beautiful colors', '2004-12-04 21:22:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046488, 124665, 10818, '<td valign="top">Very cool Blacksmith shot.  Great old huge anvil.  Would look great in black and white too.</td>', 'Very cool Blacksmith shot.  Great old huge anvil.  Would look great in black and white too.', '2004-12-04 22:06:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046490, 122857, 10818, '<td valign="top">Very interesting old water wheel...nice shot.</td>', 'Very interesting old water wheel...nice shot.', '2004-12-04 22:07:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046493, 124572, 10818, '<td valign="top">Great lines and colors and nifty idea...very nice.</td>', 'Great lines and colors and nifty idea...very nice.', '2004-12-04 22:13:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046499, 123029, 10818, '<td valign="top">Fabulous...awesome entry...well thought out and great composition.  10</td>', 'Fabulous...awesome entry...well thought out and great composition.  10', '2004-12-04 22:18:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046501, 122882, 10818, '<td valign="top">What a nice old water wheel...lots of interest, well done composition...not sure why it is sorta green....but looks good.</td>', 'What a nice old water wheel...lots of interest, well done composition...not sure why it is sorta green....but looks good.', '2004-12-04 22:23:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046505, 123484, 10818, '<td valign="top">Wheres the tap?<br/> <br/>Great shot....cool old typewriter, great high key shot.</td>', 'Wheres the tap? Great shot....cool old typewriter, great high key shot.', '2004-12-04 22:27:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046514, 123451, 10818, '<td valign="top">What a great shot.  Superb interest level and just so different....but in a good way.  The lamps really draw your eyes perfectly from top to bottom.  10</td>', 'What a great shot.  Superb interest level and just so different....but in a good way.  The lamps really draw your eyes perfectly from top to bottom.  10', '2004-12-04 22:35:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046541, 123659, 30244, '<td valign="top">Nice... very nice photo!  Top stuff!</td>', 'Nice... very nice photo!  Top stuff!', '2004-12-04 23:13:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046557, 124280, 12573, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting composition, but the actual size of the JPG is hurting you here.  I think given a larger version, your score would have been a point higher on average.  I commend the effort and the DOF (depth of field) is quite nice.  The context of what appears to be a table saw in the background should be more prominent, to show the contrast between the new and old methods of sawing.</td>', 'This is an interesting composition, but the actual size of the JPG is hurting you here.  I think given a larger version, your score would have been a point higher on average.  I commend the effort and the DOF (depth of field) is quite nice.  The context of what appears to be a table saw in the background should be more prominent, to show the contrast between the new and old methods of sawing.', '2004-12-04 23:31:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046561, 121763, 12573, '<td valign="top">Fairly good composition, but one has to ask how well it meets the challenge of "Low" tech.  I suppose the concept of low tech is a relative thing and, indeed, in 100 years I believe we will look back on the SLR camera and consider low tech.  I like the crop of this picture but I don''t like the darkness at the upper right in the background.  I''d rather see a white background and perhaps a little colored light falling on the "Fujica" body.  Good effort. 6</td>', 'Fairly good composition, but one has to ask how well it meets the challenge of "Low" tech.  I suppose the concept of low tech is a relative thing and, indeed, in 100 years I believe we will look back on the SLR camera and consider low tech.  I like the crop of this picture but I don''t like the darkness at the upper right in the background.  I''d rather see a white background and perhaps a little colored light falling on the "Fujica" body.  Good effort. 6', '2004-12-04 23:34:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046573, 124447, 12573, '<td valign="top">A classic scene that definitely fits the challenge in our current era of technology (certainly wouldn''t have been low tech 200 years ago).  The movement of the wheel and water is awkward.  I think you should have either bumped up the shutter speed and captured everything perfectly still or gone longer and had more motion than you have.  Also, rather than have nothing in the foreground, I would have like to have seen some mossy rocks or something that lets me into the scene before, Bam, I''m presented with the watermill wheel.  The sky and trees in the background add little to the scene.  Crop them out and you have a much nicer shot.  Hope that was helpful...  :)</td>', 'A classic scene that definitely fits the challenge in our current era of technology (certainly wouldn''t have been low tech 200 years ago).  The movement of the wheel and water is awkward.  I think you should have either bumped up the shutter speed and captured everything perfectly still or gone longer and had more motion than you have.  Also, rather than have nothing in the foreground, I would have like to have seen some mossy rocks or something that lets me into the scene before, Bam, I''m presented with the watermill wheel.  The sky and trees in the background add little to the scene.  Crop them out and you have a much nicer shot.  Hope that was helpful...  :)', '2004-12-04 23:40:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046575, 124819, 12573, '<td valign="top">This is my favorite kind of photography.  You''ve captured a mood with this photograph excellently.  It''s a very charming scene that looks right out of the turn of the century.  I wish only that the bowl and mixer weren''t quite so centered in the frame.  Perhaps zooming out a little and placing the bowl more the left would have helped.  It''s still a seven, since I''m a sucker for cookbook-ish photography.</td>', 'This is my favorite kind of photography.  You''ve captured a mood with this photograph excellently.  It''s a very charming scene that looks right out of the turn of the century.  I wish only that the bowl and mixer weren''t quite so centered in the frame.  Perhaps zooming out a little and placing the bowl more the left would have helped.  It''s still a seven, since I''m a sucker for cookbook-ish photography.', '2004-12-04 23:42:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046580, 123717, 12573, '<td valign="top">The bright background is a distraction.  The peeled apple looks very good in the lighting provided, though, and I like the placement of the other apples in the scene.  The cutting marks on the wood in the foreground sort of cheapen the effort you went through to set this up.  A 75% crop beginning in the left center of the image and just getting the tool handle would have improved this.  It''s still a nice effort. 6.</td>', 'The bright background is a distraction.  The peeled apple looks very good in the lighting provided, though, and I like the placement of the other apples in the scene.  The cutting marks on the wood in the foreground sort of cheapen the effort you went through to set this up.  A 75% crop beginning in the left center of the image and just getting the tool handle would have improved this.  It''s still a nice effort. 6.', '2004-12-04 23:45:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046586, 124189, 12573, '<td valign="top">I''m just having a hard time placing this picture in any context.  I understand that the "low tech" portion is the use of a candle to read by, but you must remember that the image must stand alone outside of DPC as a memorable and meaningful image.  I don''t feel anything when I look at your candle, for instance.  It looks like a candle I have on my coffee table.  An old kerosene lantern would have improved it.  Or maybe use the same candle but show us a warm mountain lodge in the background with a fire going and a dog curled up at the reader''s toes.  You are on to something with the topic being portrayed here (I would call it "Rockwellian" simplicity), but you need to tell more of a story.  Technically, there''s nothing wrong with the photo.  Exposure, composition, and lighting are all acceptable.  Just tell me a story. :)</td>', 'I''m just having a hard time placing this picture in any context.  I understand that the "low tech" portion is the use of a candle to read by, but you must remember that the image must stand alone outside of DPC as a memorable and meaningful image.  I don''t feel anything when I look at your candle, for instance.  It looks like a candle I have on my coffee table.  An old kerosene lantern would have improved it.  Or maybe use the same candle but show us a warm mountain lodge in the background with a fire going and a dog curled up at the reader''s toes.  You are on to something with the topic being portrayed here (I would call it "Rockwellian" simplicity), but you need to tell more of a story.  Technically, there''s nothing wrong with the photo.  Exposure, composition, and lighting are all acceptable.  Just tell me a story. :)', '2004-12-04 23:52:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046590, 124042, 12573, '<td valign="top">I really enjoyed this.  I love food photography and your choice of white rice here is perfect, as it tends to be less interesting that the chopsticks, which is the subject of the photo.  There is a little noise in the image that doesn''t really add anything for me.  The composition is truly great, though. 9</td>', 'I really enjoyed this.  I love food photography and your choice of white rice here is perfect, as it tends to be less interesting that the chopsticks, which is the subject of the photo.  There is a little noise in the image that doesn''t really add anything for me.  The composition is truly great, though. 9', '2004-12-04 23:57:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046594, 124666, 12573, '<td valign="top">Way to think out of the box!  Stairs are indeed about as low tech as it gets.  The position of the camera relative to the stairs here is great, as it properly shows the scale and position of the staircase.  Still, with the harsh light coming from the corner so forcefully, I''m really distracted and my eye keeps going to the light instead of the the stairs.  I think a daytime capture of this same scene would do much better.</td>', 'Way to think out of the box!  Stairs are indeed about as low tech as it gets.  The position of the camera relative to the stairs here is great, as it properly shows the scale and position of the staircase.  Still, with the harsh light coming from the corner so forcefully, I''m really distracted and my eye keeps going to the light instead of the the stairs.  I think a daytime capture of this same scene would do much better.', '2004-12-04 23:59:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046621, 123794, 12253, '<td valign="top">A simple shot of a pretty low tech common device.  The title is funny, and the shallow DOF works here.  It would make a good stock photo.</td>', 'A simple shot of a pretty low tech common device.  The title is funny, and the shallow DOF works here.  It would make a good stock photo.', '2004-12-05 00:25:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046625, 124464, 12253, '<td valign="top">The B&amp;W treatment here is good, and the tones in the foreground wonderful.  However, the ''subject'' is relegated to the background here--both in distance and in terms of the focal point, and that weakens it.  Without the caption, I would not have a clue what was being proposed here as low tech.  While it''s a beautiful photo, try to look at your photos as a "third party" and see if they tell the story you want.</td>', 'The B&W treatment here is good, and the tones in the foreground wonderful.  However, the ''subject'' is relegated to the background here--both in distance and in terms of the focal point, and that weakens it.  Without the caption, I would not have a clue what was being proposed here as low tech.  While it''s a beautiful photo, try to look at your photos as a "third party" and see if they tell the story you want.', '2004-12-05 00:28:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046628, 122552, 12253, '<td valign="top">Nice symmetry; I like the idea to do this high key, but the predominance of non-white tones in the background area lessen the impact that a brighter background would have had.</td>', 'Nice symmetry; I like the idea to do this high key, but the predominance of non-white tones in the background area lessen the impact that a brighter background would have had.', '2004-12-05 00:30:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046631, 123656, 12253, '<td valign="top">Looks low tech; not sure what it is--art work?  I suggest in the future when shooting something like this you try moving it away from the background.  Also, the photo looks like it could be leveled (blacks/whites adjusted) and focused better.</td>', 'Looks low tech; not sure what it is--art work?  I suggest in the future when shooting something like this you try moving it away from the background.  Also, the photo looks like it could be leveled (blacks/whites adjusted) and focused better.', '2004-12-05 00:34:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046633, 122686, 12253, '<td valign="top">Interesting angle and overall pretty good shot (a biit of reflected glare--hard to control with a metal surface like this.  I am not familiar with these but the "paper" like thing on the right inside detracts a bit from this shot as one of form.</td>', 'Interesting angle and overall pretty good shot (a biit of reflected glare--hard to control with a metal surface like this.  I am not familiar with these but the "paper" like thing on the right inside detracts a bit from this shot as one of form.', '2004-12-05 00:36:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046635, 124942, 18799, '<td valign="top">This needs something to separate it from the background.  More contrast, DOF, different angle, color - I''m not sure what the solution is.  As for the concept of low tech, it certainly fits.  5</td>', 'This needs something to separate it from the background.  More contrast, DOF, different angle, color - I''m not sure what the solution is.  As for the concept of low tech, it certainly fits.  5', '2004-12-05 00:38:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046639, 124707, 18799, '<td valign="top">I really like the subject.  The treatment in post, on the other hand...... not so crazy about</td>', 'I really like the subject.  The treatment in post, on the other hand...... not so crazy about', '2004-12-05 00:43:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046649, 124888, 18799, '<td valign="top">Wonderful.  Terrific perspective.  9</td>', 'Wonderful.  Terrific perspective.  9', '2004-12-05 00:48:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046830, 124788, 28261, '<td valign="top">Very sharp and nice dof.  The glasses however seem out of place, either too far off the frame or not far enough.  The handle color of the screwdriver seems to be reflecting so much light that it looks broken.</td>', 'Very sharp and nice dof.  The glasses however seem out of place, either too far off the frame or not far enough.  The handle color of the screwdriver seems to be reflecting so much light that it looks broken.', '2004-12-05 07:05:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046831, 124893, 28261, '<td valign="top">Sharp and good focus.  Seems like another simple snapshot of a child at play, perhaps a much tighter crop would raise the importance of the wagon as the subject.</td>', 'Sharp and good focus.  Seems like another simple snapshot of a child at play, perhaps a much tighter crop would raise the importance of the wagon as the subject.', '2004-12-05 07:08:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046833, 124776, 28261, '<td valign="top">Very nice use of black, white, grey without desaturation.  All elements seem in focus except top left corner which seems natural in this composition.  Just the right amount ouf saturation in the shadows to make the paper stand out.  Great concept and interesting subject matter.</td>', 'Very nice use of black, white, grey without desaturation.  All elements seem in focus except top left corner which seems natural in this composition.  Just the right amount ouf saturation in the shadows to make the paper stand out.  Great concept and interesting subject matter.', '2004-12-05 07:11:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046835, 124335, 28261, '<td valign="top">Seems to be stretching the challenge subject and details quite a bit.  Had it not been for the title I would have wondered what this had to do with technology at all.  The plastic does a great job of defocusing the background but tends to make the fingerprint look even more unreal.</td>', 'Seems to be stretching the challenge subject and details quite a bit.  Had it not been for the title I would have wondered what this had to do with technology at all.  The plastic does a great job of defocusing the background but tends to make the fingerprint look even more unreal.', '2004-12-05 07:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046836, 122775, 28261, '<td valign="top">I dont normally place bridge engineering in the technology realm, however after careful consideration of the image, can see that the support structure really is something that is very outdated for train trestles.  I give you points for the subject, but still find it less ''low tech'' and more ''old design''  Your focus is great, good DOF, bit distracting far background, but not so much that it would seems deductable.  Nice use of the banks as a framing tool.</td>', 'I dont normally place bridge engineering in the technology realm, however after careful consideration of the image, can see that the support structure really is something that is very outdated for train trestles.  I give you points for the subject, but still find it less ''low tech'' and more ''old design''  Your focus is great, good DOF, bit distracting far background, but not so much that it would seems deductable.  Nice use of the banks as a framing tool.', '2004-12-05 07:22:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046837, 123659, 28261, '<td valign="top">Really like the selective desaturation and shallow DOF making the subject really stand out.  Crop seems right on and balanced.  Hate her glasses and the pink really clashes with the rest of the composition, but you can''t be faulted too much for fashion faux pas.  I think tho I would have asked her if I could take a picture of the taxi without her on it...</td>', 'Really like the selective desaturation and shallow DOF making the subject really stand out.  Crop seems right on and balanced.  Hate her glasses and the pink really clashes with the rest of the composition, but you can''t be faulted too much for fashion faux pas.  I think tho I would have asked her if I could take a picture of the taxi without her on it...', '2004-12-05 07:26:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046838, 124905, 28261, '<td valign="top">Definitely low tech!  Excellent DOF on this and nice choice to use a new and not a ''ratty old'' trap that would have taken something away.  The mouse hole is very fuzzy on the inside edge which really flattens the image.  I''m not sure how to fix that, but it seems out of place.</td>', 'Definitely low tech!  Excellent DOF on this and nice choice to use a new and not a ''ratty old'' trap that would have taken something away.  The mouse hole is very fuzzy on the inside edge which really flattens the image.  I''m not sure how to fix that, but it seems out of place.', '2004-12-05 07:30:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046839, 124572, 28261, '<td valign="top">Old fashioned or low tech?... both.  Nice job of picking a good subject and great angle for presenting it.  Just enough DOF and focus in the center that my eyes go right to the central knot and really have a hard time not staying there!</td>', 'Old fashioned or low tech?... both.  Nice job of picking a good subject and great angle for presenting it.  Just enough DOF and focus in the center that my eyes go right to the central knot and really have a hard time not staying there!', '2004-12-05 07:32:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046841, 124832, 28261, '<td valign="top">This is a huge stretch on the technology even on low tech.  I like the textures you were able to capture on the fabric, really think the pin and paper need to go.  This would make a good E-Bay ad image, but in the challenge I fear it does not place well with me.</td>', 'This is a huge stretch on the technology even on low tech.  I like the textures you were able to capture on the fabric, really think the pin and paper need to go.  This would make a good E-Bay ad image, but in the challenge I fear it does not place well with me.', '2004-12-05 07:36:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046844, 124904, 28261, '<td valign="top">Great choice of low tech! Like the angles and offsets of the grid, sheath and rule.  Everything seems balanced well and DOF is deep but nto distracting at all.  The lighting has somehow caused the flap on the sheath to appear greenish as opposed to the black of the rest of the leather and this is very distracting.  Not sure if that could be fixed with movement of lighting or in post-process. Overall very good image tho.</td>', 'Great choice of low tech! Like the angles and offsets of the grid, sheath and rule.  Everything seems balanced well and DOF is deep but nto distracting at all.  The lighting has somehow caused the flap on the sheath to appear greenish as opposed to the black of the rest of the leather and this is very distracting.  Not sure if that could be fixed with movement of lighting or in post-process. Overall very good image tho.', '2004-12-05 07:45:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046846, 123626, 28261, '<td valign="top">Good choice of grey toothbrush as it seems to work well with the greyish complexion and very shallow dof.  I fund the image disturbing in a way, but it is well balanced.  I find very littte here to remind me of technology even low or ancient tech.  My wife says sonicare, but even that seems a stretch here.  No points for challenge, but points for composition and color.</td>', 'Good choice of grey toothbrush as it seems to work well with the greyish complexion and very shallow dof.  I fund the image disturbing in a way, but it is well balanced.  I find very littte here to remind me of technology even low or ancient tech.  My wife says sonicare, but even that seems a stretch here.  No points for challenge, but points for composition and color.', '2004-12-05 07:48:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046847, 122857, 28261, '<td valign="top">Nice choice of subject.  Definitely low technology.  Great focal point and DOF.  Something in the contrast between the wetness of the wheel and the desaturation has made the image seem more of a miniature (model) wheel rather than the real thing.  Perhaps a reversed desat would still focus on the wheel while correcting this.</td>', 'Nice choice of subject.  Definitely low technology.  Great focal point and DOF.  Something in the contrast between the wetness of the wheel and the desaturation has made the image seem more of a miniature (model) wheel rather than the real thing.  Perhaps a reversed desat would still focus on the wheel while correcting this.', '2004-12-05 07:51:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046849, 124603, 28261, '<td valign="top">This is a great image, but all wrong.  The microphone is wireless and the headset is some of the newest tech in the industry.  On the plus side, the color is brilliant, the focus spot on and the balance of subject with negative space is perfect.  Some highlights in the color and cuff are way too washed out.  This is a 3 based on challenge, not composition.</td>', 'This is a great image, but all wrong.  The microphone is wireless and the headset is some of the newest tech in the industry.  On the plus side, the color is brilliant, the focus spot on and the balance of subject with negative space is perfect.  Some highlights in the color and cuff are way too washed out.  This is a 3 based on challenge, not composition.', '2004-12-05 07:54:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046850, 123085, 28261, '<td valign="top">I''ll grant its low tech, lighters are higher tech, but a magnifying glass would have been super low tech.  Other than that, I find the subject''s presentation too simplified.  The DOF is not deep enough to keep the single match head in focus on the outer rim of the field.  Moving the match head to the center would fix this, but would not save the whole which seems more like a shot that would be taken in a digital camera scavenger hunt - go find some matches, not find something low tech, and still not interesting enough for a stock photograph.</td>', 'I''ll grant its low tech, lighters are higher tech, but a magnifying glass would have been super low tech.  Other than that, I find the subject''s presentation too simplified.  The DOF is not deep enough to keep the single match head in focus on the outer rim of the field.  Moving the match head to the center would fix this, but would not save the whole which seems more like a shot that would be taken in a digital camera scavenger hunt - go find some matches, not find something low tech, and still not interesting enough for a stock photograph.', '2004-12-05 08:00:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046879, 122686, 28261, '<td valign="top">Definitely low tech.  The angle seems a bit too steep for my personal liking, but that seems too subjective to really be a factor.  I like the DOF here with the subject very focused and the wood slightly blurred.  Highlight on the central body seems too striking, but still high marks for this one.</td>', 'Definitely low tech.  The angle seems a bit too steep for my personal liking, but that seems too subjective to really be a factor.  I like the DOF here with the subject very focused and the wood slightly blurred.  Highlight on the central body seems too striking, but still high marks for this one.', '2004-12-05 09:34:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046880, 122472, 28261, '<td valign="top">High key sepia tone, interesting.  Unfortunately makes me think I need to recalibrate my monitor again as much of the back seems simply overexposed or under contrasted.  I don''t think of technology at all with the subject matter, but can see the interpretation when compared to current day footwear.  The border is effective, but I didn''t really feel the subject as quite fitting the challenge.</td>', 'High key sepia tone, interesting.  Unfortunately makes me think I need to recalibrate my monitor again as much of the back seems simply overexposed or under contrasted.  I don''t think of technology at all with the subject matter, but can see the interpretation when compared to current day footwear.  The border is effective, but I didn''t really feel the subject as quite fitting the challenge.', '2004-12-05 09:38:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046881, 124586, 28261, '<td valign="top">Crop left wide-angle corner artifacts which are very distracting.  The subject is hard to see due to the small size of the photograph (should use the whole 640 allowed if possible).  Overall seems to fit teh challenge, but not interesting or large enough to make it above average.</td>', 'Crop left wide-angle corner artifacts which are very distracting.  The subject is hard to see due to the small size of the photograph (should use the whole 640 allowed if possible).  Overall seems to fit teh challenge, but not interesting or large enough to make it above average.', '2004-12-05 09:40:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046882, 124853, 28261, '<td valign="top">Low tech compared to modern sticky envelopes, but not really invoking a sense of technology.  Neither the wax nor an envelope seems to lead me to thinking of technology.  I do really like the DOF here and the leading of the stamp to point at the wax.  Both are very crisp and the shadows are just enough to not leave the objects floating in negative space.  Would make a great wall hanging, but would not categorize as low technology.</td>', 'Low tech compared to modern sticky envelopes, but not really invoking a sense of technology.  Neither the wax nor an envelope seems to lead me to thinking of technology.  I do really like the DOF here and the leading of the stamp to point at the wax.  Both are very crisp and the shadows are just enough to not leave the objects floating in negative space.  Would make a great wall hanging, but would not categorize as low technology.', '2004-12-05 09:43:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046885, 124115, 28261, '<td valign="top">I really like the reflection and spot on straightness of the focal point.  Leads the candle to appear a lot larger than a simple tea candle and this draws the eye right to the focus.  The softness of the inside hands also brings the eye to the flame and the long exposure star highlights are very effective.  The ''x-ray'' effect on the fingers is somewhat distracting, but the gradual push into the shadows seems to mostly nullify that.  Very impressive composition and a top contender in my book.</td>', 'I really like the reflection and spot on straightness of the focal point.  Leads the candle to appear a lot larger than a simple tea candle and this draws the eye right to the focus.  The softness of the inside hands also brings the eye to the flame and the long exposure star highlights are very effective.  The ''x-ray'' effect on the fingers is somewhat distracting, but the gradual push into the shadows seems to mostly nullify that.  Very impressive composition and a top contender in my book.', '2004-12-05 09:46:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046893, 122505, 28261, '<td valign="top">Although alone the tools don''t say or imply technology to me, together and against the background of aged wood, they seem to fit into a ''low tech'' arena, reminding me of waterwheels, old wagons and thusly low tech.  I like the crop of the shovel especially as it somehow lends to the subtracting nature of the rest of the line.  Wondering what the whole would have looked like if you shot the shovel in the center, implying an arrow or triangular shape between the uprights.  Well centered.  The lower left item that seems to have been cloned out is very distracting, like a burnt piece of wood that should have been removed first.  There also seems to be a halo of oversharpening on the garden claw but not so much that it in a larger print it would be distracting.   I like this interpretation of the challenge and give high marks.</td>', 'Although alone the tools don''t say or imply technology to me, together and against the background of aged wood, they seem to fit into a ''low tech'' arena, reminding me of waterwheels, old wagons and thusly low tech.  I like the crop of the shovel especially as it somehow lends to the subtracting nature of the rest of the line.  Wondering what the whole would have looked like if you shot the shovel in the center, implying an arrow or triangular shape between the uprights.  Well centered.  The lower left item that seems to have been cloned out is very distracting, like a burnt piece of wood that should have been removed first.  There also seems to be a halo of oversharpening on the garden claw but not so much that it in a larger print it would be distracting.   I like this interpretation of the challenge and give high marks.', '2004-12-05 09:53:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046899, 122388, 28261, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful picture, well framed and just enough DOF to lift it out of the black.  It is well lit and the ribbon placed well in the overall shot.  I could not suggest any improvements on it at all and this would make a great wall hanging or stock photo, but does not invoke low tech to me at all as I see no technology in tea pots in general.  Instead it says to me ancient culture.  High marks for composition, some loss for challenge interpretation.</td>', 'This is a beautiful picture, well framed and just enough DOF to lift it out of the black.  It is well lit and the ribbon placed well in the overall shot.  I could not suggest any improvements on it at all and this would make a great wall hanging or stock photo, but does not invoke low tech to me at all as I see no technology in tea pots in general.  Instead it says to me ancient culture.  High marks for composition, some loss for challenge interpretation.', '2004-12-05 09:56:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046904, 124592, 28261, '<td valign="top">I see clearly the link to technology here as tanks and other gunnery have definitely evloved through higher tech.  The decay/dust on the top of the cannon (with the additional avian highlights) detracts from the composition, but unless you were going to stand there and polish the thing cannot fault you for that at all.  Nice DOF, framing and use of natural lighting.  In some ways the forward wheel seems a bit to smooth to invoke age and this could be a result of overdoing the noise reduction or perhaps blurring based on DOF.  Overall a very pleasant pic with well placed shadow and highlight.  Perhaps actually adding some grain to the image would be worth investigating.  Good strong marks all around.</td>', 'I see clearly the link to technology here as tanks and other gunnery have definitely evloved through higher tech.  The decay/dust on the top of the cannon (with the additional avian highlights) detracts from the composition, but unless you were going to stand there and polish the thing cannot fault you for that at all.  Nice DOF, framing and use of natural lighting.  In some ways the forward wheel seems a bit to smooth to invoke age and this could be a result of overdoing the noise reduction or perhaps blurring based on DOF.  Overall a very pleasant pic with well placed shadow and highlight.  Perhaps actually adding some grain to the image would be worth investigating.  Good strong marks all around.', '2004-12-05 10:01:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046906, 124707, 28261, '<td valign="top">Defined by low tech, but seems to be saturated or color hue corrected to the point of appearing very oversampled.  Perhaps this is an artistic presentation of the subject, but the grain of the wood has become ''cartoonish'' while the blue-green of the background is distracting beyond the art.  Fits the challenge well, but the other elements seriously detract from the presentation.  Perhaps a larger block of wood and less background would draw my eye to the drill which I found to be almost secondary to the presentation.</td>', 'Defined by low tech, but seems to be saturated or color hue corrected to the point of appearing very oversampled.  Perhaps this is an artistic presentation of the subject, but the grain of the wood has become ''cartoonish'' while the blue-green of the background is distracting beyond the art.  Fits the challenge well, but the other elements seriously detract from the presentation.  Perhaps a larger block of wood and less background would draw my eye to the drill which I found to be almost secondary to the presentation.', '2004-12-05 10:05:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046910, 123235, 28261, '<td valign="top">A great presentation of low tech.  This is well framed all the way from the palcement of the drill and angle to the board and its angle.  A little shadowy on the top handball and somewhat overexposed in the left part of the board, but really a pleasant and well composed image.  Good strong high marks on this.</td>', 'A great presentation of low tech.  This is well framed all the way from the palcement of the drill and angle to the board and its angle.  A little shadowy on the top handball and somewhat overexposed in the left part of the board, but really a pleasant and well composed image.  Good strong high marks on this.', '2004-12-05 10:08:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046918, 124525, 28261, '<td valign="top">Electrical yes.  Electronic...doesn''t seem so much.  Low tech-definitely  Sepia toning greatly enhances the ''aging'' of this image and it is well-framed but seems too busy.  The butter on the lower corner and ''bagel?bread?" on the right center are way overexposed as is the upper left corner; perhaps tho this is something akin to kigh-key antique style.  Compared to the dark, rich tone in the toaster, it seems a bit out of place.  Clean out some of the distractions and simplify the whole to create a real impact, but overall a good presentation of the challenge.</td>', 'Electrical yes.  Electronic...doesn''t seem so much.  Low tech-definitely  Sepia toning greatly enhances the ''aging'' of this image and it is well-framed but seems too busy.  The butter on the lower corner and ''bagel?bread?" on the right center are way overexposed as is the upper left corner; perhaps tho this is something akin to kigh-key antique style.  Compared to the dark, rich tone in the toaster, it seems a bit out of place.  Clean out some of the distractions and simplify the whole to create a real impact, but overall a good presentation of the challenge.', '2004-12-05 10:12:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046923, 124906, 28261, '<td valign="top">Hmm...building blocks, compared to what?  Toys? brick and mortar? Granite? Steel?  I don''t really see low technology here, but I do see a great abstract composition.  I like the choice of primary colors and the arrangement of the blocks.  The framing and crop are perfect, but the shadows are too deep and detract from the color impact.  DOF and focus seem just right and the square crop shape is a good subtle contrast to the rectangular forms.  (Very) hgh marks on composition, low marks on challenge interpretation.</td>', 'Hmm...building blocks, compared to what?  Toys? brick and mortar? Granite? Steel?  I don''t really see low technology here, but I do see a great abstract composition.  I like the choice of primary colors and the arrangement of the blocks.  The framing and crop are perfect, but the shadows are too deep and detract from the color impact.  DOF and focus seem just right and the square crop shape is a good subtle contrast to the rectangular forms.  (Very) hgh marks on composition, low marks on challenge interpretation.', '2004-12-05 10:16:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046926, 124697, 28261, '<td valign="top">Low technology, no electronics.  Hmmm....I see a great b/w composition of an aged/abandoned building and a tractor, but this does not seem to invoke technology to me, even low tech, in some ways, the tractor almost contrasts the age of the building, making it seem higher tech than the rest of the picture.   The tones are great, framiing and crop right on, but the subject matter seems could be confusing in the realm of low tech.</td>', 'Low technology, no electronics.  Hmmm....I see a great b/w composition of an aged/abandoned building and a tractor, but this does not seem to invoke technology to me, even low tech, in some ways, the tractor almost contrasts the age of the building, making it seem higher tech than the rest of the picture.   The tones are great, framiing and crop right on, but the subject matter seems could be confusing in the realm of low tech.', '2004-12-05 10:20:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046928, 122959, 28261, '<td valign="top">This is a very solid image.  The focus is dead on, textures are bold, hand markings are a striking contrast to the scrathes on the knife.  There seems to be an overabundance of Dodging on the forward hand''s fingers in the shadowy area and this is very distracting.  I do not see low tech here except in comparision to a pencil sharpener, but pencil sharpeners don''t really invoke ideas of technological advancement to me.  Some very strong points in this overall, one major distraction and something of a leap (for me) on the challenge itself.</td>', 'This is a very solid image.  The focus is dead on, textures are bold, hand markings are a striking contrast to the scrathes on the knife.  There seems to be an overabundance of Dodging on the forward hand''s fingers in the shadowy area and this is very distracting.  I do not see low tech here except in comparision to a pencil sharpener, but pencil sharpeners don''t really invoke ideas of technological advancement to me.  Some very strong points in this overall, one major distraction and something of a leap (for me) on the challenge itself.', '2004-12-05 10:24:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046933, 122552, 28261, '<td valign="top">An impressive high-key ''color'' image.  Very artistisic presentation, well balanced and framed/cropped.  Te contrasts seem a bit harsh, but could be expected.  I do not find it hard to relate this to low tech comparing to other modes of boating (motorized, cruise ships) although the technology inference does require some interpretation.</td>', 'An impressive high-key ''color'' image.  Very artistisic presentation, well balanced and framed/cropped.  Te contrasts seem a bit harsh, but could be expected.  I do not find it hard to relate this to low tech comparing to other modes of boating (motorized, cruise ships) although the technology inference does require some interpretation.', '2004-12-05 10:29:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046936, 123975, 28261, '<td valign="top">The image presented does not invoke technology to me at all, although the title may infer some kind of static removel device.  It is presented in much too small an area (not 640) to really compete with other images, but the composition is well balanced in the area presented.</td>', 'The image presented does not invoke technology to me at all, although the title may infer some kind of static removel device.  It is presented in much too small an area (not 640) to really compete with other images, but the composition is well balanced in the area presented.', '2004-12-05 10:32:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046981, 124974, 28261, '<td valign="top">Hmm...first vote and comment did not stay, so here goes again...<br/> <br/>Nice border and use of negative space.  Watch is an easy link to low tech for me.  Highlights on the fob ring and shadows on the bottom of the watch were eyecatching to me.  I liked the way the light caught the crystal, reflecting the scratch and giving the glass presence.  Missing second hand is distracting, but not something that affects the score.  Overall a high marking image.</td>', 'Hmm...first vote and comment did not stay, so here goes again... Nice border and use of negative space.  Watch is an easy link to low tech for me.  Highlights on the fob ring and shadows on the bottom of the watch were eyecatching to me.  I liked the way the light caught the crystal, reflecting the scratch and giving the glass presence.  Missing second hand is distracting, but not something that affects the score.  Overall a high marking image.', '2004-12-05 11:54:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046983, 124665, 28261, '<td valign="top">Although this image is somewhat busy, the inferenece to low technology or at least old ways is very clear here.  Good job of catching light in what seems a low light circumstance (fill flash?) I think a tight crop would make this a more artistic and improve the presentation, but find the link to the challenge to be very solid.</td>', 'Although this image is somewhat busy, the inferenece to low technology or at least old ways is very clear here.  Good job of catching light in what seems a low light circumstance (fill flash?) I think a tight crop would make this a more artistic and improve the presentation, but find the link to the challenge to be very solid.', '2004-12-05 11:57:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046985, 124623, 28261, '<td valign="top">That piece of metal is just gross looking!  It would be hard to choke down the meal that it opened.  Great low tech choice, no interpretation needed.  The framing and crop is fine as is the DOF, but the subjects have a turn off factor that rivals the message.  You should take a Dremel or Brillo, clean up the can opener, peel the label off the can and reshoot a black and white with maximum impact.  Very high marks for challenge interpretation and composition, some deduction for subject that makes me want to wash dishes.</td>', 'That piece of metal is just gross looking!  It would be hard to choke down the meal that it opened.  Great low tech choice, no interpretation needed.  The framing and crop is fine as is the DOF, but the subjects have a turn off factor that rivals the message.  You should take a Dremel or Brillo, clean up the can opener, peel the label off the can and reshoot a black and white with maximum impact.  Very high marks for challenge interpretation and composition, some deduction for subject that makes me want to wash dishes.', '2004-12-05 12:04:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046988, 123697, 28261, '<td valign="top">Unsure if this is galvanized, green paint, or silver.  Very interesting texture to the whole and well framed.  Something in the depth of the subject on the head of the key is casting greyish shadows on the side and in the holes.  This is very distracting.  I see no real technology in a key or in current key use/design, but can see the implied technology of advancement in security and find that with some interpretation that this subject fits the challenge artistically.  Average marks on all levels: challenge, composition and cleanness of image.  Extra points for a subject that has an interesting texture and form.</td>', 'Unsure if this is galvanized, green paint, or silver.  Very interesting texture to the whole and well framed.  Something in the depth of the subject on the head of the key is casting greyish shadows on the side and in the holes.  This is very distracting.  I see no real technology in a key or in current key use/design, but can see the implied technology of advancement in security and find that with some interpretation that this subject fits the challenge artistically.  Average marks on all levels: challenge, composition and cleanness of image.  Extra points for a subject that has an interesting texture and form.', '2004-12-05 12:08:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046991, 124819, 28261, '<td valign="top">I like everything about this picture.  The framing in a square offsetting the roundness of the subject, the mild sepia toning and the modern-feel fo the crisp, sharpness in the image as a whole.  The cookbook and radio (yikes I see electronics!) in no way impact the real subject of the hand mixer, in fact, they are such an after thought as to be a perfect background.  Nice Job: a top contender!</td>', 'I like everything about this picture.  The framing in a square offsetting the roundness of the subject, the mild sepia toning and the modern-feel fo the crisp, sharpness in the image as a whole.  The cookbook and radio (yikes I see electronics!) in no way impact the real subject of the hand mixer, in fact, they are such an after thought as to be a perfect background.  Nice Job: a top contender!', '2004-12-05 12:11:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046995, 124858, 28261, '<td valign="top">When I see camera''s of this style and 8mm movie cameras in general, I cannot help but to think of early electronics.  These were the ''gadgets'' of the day.  Certainly low-tech as the challenge title implies, but outside fo the challenge as the details instruct.  Otherwise, this is a fabulous portrait of some toys of yesteryear.  The balance of box vs box+camera, framing the starmite is very nice.  A little too much light behind the yellow box, making the background a bit too noticable.  May have wanted to clone out the meeting of the wall and platform to smooth it out a bit.<br/> <br/>Overall high marks for composition, clarity of subject and detail, serious detraction for electronica.</td>', 'When I see camera''s of this style and 8mm movie cameras in general, I cannot help but to think of early electronics.  These were the ''gadgets'' of the day.  Certainly low-tech as the challenge title implies, but outside fo the challenge as the details instruct.  Otherwise, this is a fabulous portrait of some toys of yesteryear.  The balance of box vs box+camera, framing the starmite is very nice.  A little too much light behind the yellow box, making the background a bit too noticable.  May have wanted to clone out the meeting of the wall and platform to smooth it out a bit. Overall high marks for composition, clarity of subject and detail, serious detraction for electronica.', '2004-12-05 12:16:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046998, 124876, 28261, '<td valign="top">Makes me think plumbing, but does nto make me think technology or even low technology.  This is an item that has stood the test of time over the evolution of plumbing for quite some time.  The image on the other hand is very well done: simple, focused and balanced with only the upper right section being too well lit compared to the rest of the shot.  The border is great and the perfect color.  High marks for composition and presentation, some loss on challenge interpretation from the viewer.</td>', 'Makes me think plumbing, but does nto make me think technology or even low technology.  This is an item that has stood the test of time over the evolution of plumbing for quite some time.  The image on the other hand is very well done: simple, focused and balanced with only the upper right section being too well lit compared to the rest of the shot.  The border is great and the perfect color.  High marks for composition and presentation, some loss on challenge interpretation from the viewer.', '2004-12-05 12:19:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1046999, 124487, 28261, '<td valign="top">I see no technology here at all.  Not high tech or low tech.  I see constuction and simplicity.  The image itself is well done, lighting good for the effect, but somewhere in here a ton of resampled grain and archive bits showed up.  (unless the spotting in the border and shadows was intentional for art, I found it quite distracting).  Good average for focus and detail in the subject, heavy losses for challenge interpretation and final presentation that appears mottled.</td>', 'I see no technology here at all.  Not high tech or low tech.  I see constuction and simplicity.  The image itself is well done, lighting good for the effect, but somewhere in here a ton of resampled grain and archive bits showed up.  (unless the spotting in the border and shadows was intentional for art, I found it quite distracting).  Good average for focus and detail in the subject, heavy losses for challenge interpretation and final presentation that appears mottled.', '2004-12-05 12:22:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047000, 123659, 29009, '<td valign="top">You''ve captured the expression on the girl''s face wonderfully!</td>', 'You''ve captured the expression on the girl''s face wonderfully!', '2004-12-05 12:23:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047001, 124665, 29009, '<td valign="top">This shot is awesome!  Meets challenge, visually interesting, well lit, excellent subject.  Well done!</td>', 'This shot is awesome!  Meets challenge, visually interesting, well lit, excellent subject.  Well done!', '2004-12-05 12:24:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047003, 124671, 29009, '<td valign="top">Good use of lines here.</td>', 'Good use of lines here.', '2004-12-05 12:25:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047005, 124196, 29009, '<td valign="top">Original idea.  There is an overexposed area in the lower left corner that detracts from the overall image.</td>', 'Original idea.  There is an overexposed area in the lower left corner that detracts from the overall image.', '2004-12-05 12:27:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047006, 122288, 29009, '<td valign="top">Good use of lighting to capture the shadow for visual interest.</td>', 'Good use of lighting to capture the shadow for visual interest.', '2004-12-05 12:27:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047007, 124803, 29009, '<td valign="top">Good title, original idea.  The overall shot might have benefited from a tighter crop as the focal point appears to be the house rather than the bell.</td>', 'Good title, original idea.  The overall shot might have benefited from a tighter crop as the focal point appears to be the house rather than the bell.', '2004-12-05 12:29:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047010, 124609, 29009, '<td valign="top">Good use of lines here.</td>', 'Good use of lines here.', '2004-12-05 12:30:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047012, 122330, 28261, '<td valign="top">Sextant, compass or something else?  Wow this thing looks so mechanical compared to a simple LL Bean compass that it must be low tech!  The detail in the surface scratching screams old.  I like the very tight crop and all the impurities of the subject.  The 40-10 area seemed too dodged or fuzzy as did the upper 1/3 and became a bit of a distraction as I continued to study the image, probably the only thing I would consider trying to fix, but may have simply been a factor of subject''s age and limitation of macro DOF.</td>', 'Sextant, compass or something else?  Wow this thing looks so mechanical compared to a simple LL Bean compass that it must be low tech!  The detail in the surface scratching screams old.  I like the very tight crop and all the impurities of the subject.  The 40-10 area seemed too dodged or fuzzy as did the upper 1/3 and became a bit of a distraction as I continued to study the image, probably the only thing I would consider trying to fix, but may have simply been a factor of subject''s age and limitation of macro DOF.', '2004-12-05 12:31:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047013, 122432, 29009, '<td valign="top">Oh perfect!  Excellent subject, meet challenge spot on.  Great composition and use of depth of field.  Colors are good - overall a fantastic shot!</td>', 'Oh perfect!  Excellent subject, meet challenge spot on.  Great composition and use of depth of field.  Colors are good - overall a fantastic shot!', '2004-12-05 12:31:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047018, 123063, 28261, '<td valign="top">Ancient Utensils yes.  Old Culture, not low technology.  Very nice perspective and focus on the patterns.  Texture of the table really adds to the whole as does the shallow DOF, but the highlight on the stick ends at bottom is annoying, and draws my attention there like a magnet.  Lighting and tonality otherwise get high marks, challenge interpretation from the viewer is too far removed from tech.</td>', 'Ancient Utensils yes.  Old Culture, not low technology.  Very nice perspective and focus on the patterns.  Texture of the table really adds to the whole as does the shallow DOF, but the highlight on the stick ends at bottom is annoying, and draws my attention there like a magnet.  Lighting and tonality otherwise get high marks, challenge interpretation from the viewer is too far removed from tech.', '2004-12-05 12:34:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047020, 124973, 29009, '<td valign="top">Original subject.  I''m laughing!  Find myself wishing the shot had demonstrated the use of the tape in a "fix-it" situation as that might have added visual interest.</td>', 'Original subject.  I''m laughing!  Find myself wishing the shot had demonstrated the use of the tape in a "fix-it" situation as that might have added visual interest.', '2004-12-05 12:34:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047021, 124942, 29009, '<td valign="top">Good subject.  A bit more contrast might have lifted the focal point away from the background, but overall a good shot.</td>', 'Good subject.  A bit more contrast might have lifted the focal point away from the background, but overall a good shot.', '2004-12-05 12:35:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047022, 124502, 29009, '<td valign="top">Great subject!  There''s an overall blue cast that might be distracting for some viewers....</td>', 'Great subject!  There''s an overall blue cast that might be distracting for some viewers....', '2004-12-05 12:36:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047024, 124985, 28261, '<td valign="top">I see nothing tech about this except the title.  Alone, the image says protest or revolt, wake up and realize something, but I cannot get to tech from here.  Overall an interesting and troubling picture that would have much more impact journalistically.  DOF and focus are very nice, tonality is good, crop is right on, challenge is lacking.</td>', 'I see nothing tech about this except the title.  Alone, the image says protest or revolt, wake up and realize something, but I cannot get to tech from here.  Overall an interesting and troubling picture that would have much more impact journalistically.  DOF and focus are very nice, tonality is good, crop is right on, challenge is lacking.', '2004-12-05 12:38:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047025, 123717, 29009, '<td valign="top">Great subject, excellent composition, good use of color and lighting.  Overall, a very strong shot that I hope does well.  I especially like the fact that you presented your subject actually in use - the long peel with all the curlicues adds tons of visual interest!</td>', 'Great subject, excellent composition, good use of color and lighting.  Overall, a very strong shot that I hope does well.  I especially like the fact that you presented your subject actually in use - the long peel with all the curlicues adds tons of visual interest!', '2004-12-05 12:39:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047028, 124280, 28261, '<td valign="top">The saw does not invoke a sence of technology in this presentation.  Ultimately the image is too small to seriously consider anything beyond teh most obvious that this is a picture of a saw, well framed in the given space, but somehow lacking in the presence to be of artistic or journalistic interest.</td>', 'The saw does not invoke a sence of technology in this presentation.  Ultimately the image is too small to seriously consider anything beyond teh most obvious that this is a picture of a saw, well framed in the given space, but somehow lacking in the presence to be of artistic or journalistic interest.', '2004-12-05 12:40:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047036, 123626, 29009, '<td valign="top">Well, you''ve got some definite visual interest here.  I''m not sure about how well toothpaste as a subject  meets the challenge (without the title, might have gotten confused between the paste and the modern toothbrush as a focal point), but kudos to you for originality!</td>', 'Well, you''ve got some definite visual interest here.  I''m not sure about how well toothpaste as a subject  meets the challenge (without the title, might have gotten confused between the paste and the modern toothbrush as a focal point), but kudos to you for originality!', '2004-12-05 12:43:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047037, 124524, 28261, '<td valign="top">I see a perfectly framed and cropped presentation of a stapler.  Dof is great for this composition, monochrome maximizes the impact of the shot, some specular crud showing up in the lowest right corner just in front of the last bit of stapler hinge, but it does not in any way really invoke or imply technology to me.  High marks for presentation, but a hard hit from the viewer who cannot make the leap to technology, mechanics yes, but not low tech.</td>', 'I see a perfectly framed and cropped presentation of a stapler.  Dof is great for this composition, monochrome maximizes the impact of the shot, some specular crud showing up in the lowest right corner just in front of the last bit of stapler hinge, but it does not in any way really invoke or imply technology to me.  High marks for presentation, but a hard hit from the viewer who cannot make the leap to technology, mechanics yes, but not low tech.', '2004-12-05 12:44:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047040, 122505, 29009, '<td valign="top">Excellent composition, good use of descending heights to create a visual line, good use of the studs for framing effect.</td>', 'Excellent composition, good use of descending heights to create a visual line, good use of the studs for framing effect.', '2004-12-05 12:45:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047046, 124506, 29009, '<td valign="top">Without the title, the focal point appears to be the girl and it''s not obvious that she''s holding Play-doh.  She''s very cute.  I''m not sure this photo meets the challenge as well as the other submissions.</td>', 'Without the title, the focal point appears to be the girl and it''s not obvious that she''s holding Play-doh.  She''s very cute.  I''m not sure this photo meets the challenge as well as the other submissions.', '2004-12-05 12:47:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047047, 124637, 28261, '<td valign="top">I lack any familiarty with sailing and rigging technology, but ropes and pulleys in some way do lend to the inference of technology and low technology at that.  I like the choice of subject matter in the coloring and balance of whites, blues, browns.  The angle is interesting and DOF just deep enough to draw the eye to the subject, while implying the complexity of the whole.  Very nice, by the end of this little critique, the whole had moved considerably higher than my first impression!</td>', 'I lack any familiarty with sailing and rigging technology, but ropes and pulleys in some way do lend to the inference of technology and low technology at that.  I like the choice of subject matter in the coloring and balance of whites, blues, browns.  The angle is interesting and DOF just deep enough to draw the eye to the subject, while implying the complexity of the whole.  Very nice, by the end of this little critique, the whole had moved considerably higher than my first impression!', '2004-12-05 12:47:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047053, 124603, 29009, '<td valign="top">This is a great shot, no doubt about it.  Good facial expression, good use of gradient color in the background, a very strong image.  I am marking this lower than I would like because the obvious use of electronics (wireless microphone and ear bud) does not meet the challenge topic, in my opinion.</td>', 'This is a great shot, no doubt about it.  Good facial expression, good use of gradient color in the background, a very strong image.  I am marking this lower than I would like because the obvious use of electronics (wireless microphone and ear bud) does not meet the challenge topic, in my opinion.', '2004-12-05 12:49:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047055, 124863, 29009, '<td valign="top">Great subject here.  Good composition with the fence posts leading the viewer in the same direction as the buggy.  I find myself wishing for more of the buggy than just the rear, though.  Overall, you must be pleased with the shot.</td>', 'Great subject here.  Good composition with the fence posts leading the viewer in the same direction as the buggy.  I find myself wishing for more of the buggy than just the rear, though.  Overall, you must be pleased with the shot.', '2004-12-05 12:51:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047057, 124987, 28261, '<td valign="top">Another old tool shot.  The elements are here, wood handles, age marks, simple hand mechanics and the wooden toolbox adds something to the whole, but the framing of the whole seriously detracts from the elements.  The box itself overwhelms the pieces and takes attention away from them rather than enhancing the feeling of age.  Perhaps taking all of the tools, rearranging them in only the top cubbies and closing in on the whole would have a better impact on the presentation of an otherwise good challenge interpretation.</td>', 'Another old tool shot.  The elements are here, wood handles, age marks, simple hand mechanics and the wooden toolbox adds something to the whole, but the framing of the whole seriously detracts from the elements.  The box itself overwhelms the pieces and takes attention away from them rather than enhancing the feeling of age.  Perhaps taking all of the tools, rearranging them in only the top cubbies and closing in on the whole would have a better impact on the presentation of an otherwise good challenge interpretation.', '2004-12-05 12:51:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047060, 123777, 29009, '<td valign="top">Good subject, meets challenge well.  The top left part of the opener is getting a bit lost in the background, though.</td>', 'Good subject, meets challenge well.  The top left part of the opener is getting a bit lost in the background, though.', '2004-12-05 12:53:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047061, 124785, 29009, '<td valign="top">Very creatively done.  Excellent composition using framing to demonstrate point of view.  Trap is clearly in focus, subject meets the challenge well.  I''m sure you are pleased with this shot....thanks for submitting!  It made me laugh.</td>', 'Very creatively done.  Excellent composition using framing to demonstrate point of view.  Trap is clearly in focus, subject meets the challenge well.  I''m sure you are pleased with this shot....thanks for submitting!  It made me laugh.', '2004-12-05 12:55:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047065, 123940, 28261, '<td valign="top">Sundials remind me of calculus.  Simple in nature and yet somehow quietly complex.  This image conjures those feelings again and yet it is without question mechanical and low tech at the same time.  The angle of the shot and framing in the cropped negative space is well executed.  Just the right DOF and gold on black choice only adds to the whole.  A few spots that seem over lighted and the center ''thing'' above the glass seems far too shadowy.  Overall a great interpretation of the challenge from the viewer''s seat and solid marks for composition with only a minor hit on some technical distraction.</td>', 'Sundials remind me of calculus.  Simple in nature and yet somehow quietly complex.  This image conjures those feelings again and yet it is without question mechanical and low tech at the same time.  The angle of the shot and framing in the cropped negative space is well executed.  Just the right DOF and gold on black choice only adds to the whole.  A few spots that seem over lighted and the center ''thing'' above the glass seems far too shadowy.  Overall a great interpretation of the challenge from the viewer''s seat and solid marks for composition with only a minor hit on some technical distraction.', '2004-12-05 12:56:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047068, 124697, 29009, '<td valign="top">This is a strong shot.  Your focal point is getting lost though - is it the tractor or the fireplace?  I''m assuming the tractor, since the chimney is not in use.  Black and white was a good artistic choice.</td>', 'This is a strong shot.  Your focal point is getting lost though - is it the tractor or the fireplace?  I''m assuming the tractor, since the chimney is not in use.  Black and white was a good artistic choice.', '2004-12-05 12:58:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047071, 124189, 29009, '<td valign="top">This shot doesn''t demonstrate "low-tech" without the title and knowledge of the challenge parameters.  Overall, it is a good image but I''m marking it lower than I would like because I can''t tell if the candlelight or the book is your focal point.</td>', 'This shot doesn''t demonstrate "low-tech" without the title and knowledge of the challenge parameters.  Overall, it is a good image but I''m marking it lower than I would like because I can''t tell if the candlelight or the book is your focal point.', '2004-12-05 13:02:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047072, 124981, 28261, '<td valign="top">Beyond a doubt, candlelight somehow always invokes low tech to me.  The halos around the flame are nice and soft, the smoke wispy, but not natural enough.  It appears at one point the smoke is going naturally to the high and on the candle right next to it, somewhat sideways, whereas the unlit candle''s smoke seems to be going in the opposite direction and is obviously ''been blown out''  It seems hard to evaluate the framing of the subject, and then I see the imbalance of three ''top'' candles versus the two ''bottom'' candles one of which, now unlit adds even more imbalance to the whole.  The focus and DOF in this low light shot is very good, but the smoke at the base of the candle in the center makes a blurring feature that should be removed.  I feel distracted by the elements in this shot which has a strong negative impact on the whole.</td>', 'Beyond a doubt, candlelight somehow always invokes low tech to me.  The halos around the flame are nice and soft, the smoke wispy, but not natural enough.  It appears at one point the smoke is going naturally to the high and on the candle right next to it, somewhat sideways, whereas the unlit candle''s smoke seems to be going in the opposite direction and is obviously ''been blown out''  It seems hard to evaluate the framing of the subject, and then I see the imbalance of three ''top'' candles versus the two ''bottom'' candles one of which, now unlit adds even more imbalance to the whole.  The focus and DOF in this low light shot is very good, but the smoke at the base of the candle in the center makes a blurring feature that should be removed.  I feel distracted by the elements in this shot which has a strong negative impact on the whole.', '2004-12-05 13:02:59.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1047073, 124902, 29009, '<td valign="top">Good subject, excellent use of lines!</td>', 'Good subject, excellent use of lines!', '2004-12-05 13:03:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047077, 124984, 29009, '<td valign="top">I''m not convinced this shot meets the challenge.  The subject is not as visually interesting as some of the other submissions.  Overall, it''s a decent shot but without the title it''s not clear that the mechanic is using low technology.</td>', 'I''m not convinced this shot meets the challenge.  The subject is not as visually interesting as some of the other submissions.  Overall, it''s a decent shot but without the title it''s not clear that the mechanic is using low technology.', '2004-12-05 13:07:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047080, 124394, 28261, '<td valign="top">I am not reminded of low technology when seeing this pump.  Instead, it invokes the ''good old days'' or antique sentiments, nostalgia.  The height of the pump vs the tree and the rest of the crop are well thought and create a nice balance against the 90 degree corner in the background.  The white car is a huge distraction and looks very out of place, perhaps a tighter crop would fix this, but could defeat other aspects the composition.  The green tone and overexposed sky do little to nostalgify this for me, but perhaps some grain and a sepia toning with no car would give a more solid ''old'' feel to it.</td>', 'I am not reminded of low technology when seeing this pump.  Instead, it invokes the ''good old days'' or antique sentiments, nostalgia.  The height of the pump vs the tree and the rest of the crop are well thought and create a nice balance against the 90 degree corner in the background.  The white car is a huge distraction and looks very out of place, perhaps a tighter crop would fix this, but could defeat other aspects the composition.  The green tone and overexposed sky do little to nostalgify this for me, but perhaps some grain and a sepia toning with no car would give a more solid ''old'' feel to it.', '2004-12-05 13:07:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047085, 124981, 29009, '<td valign="top">Overall, this is a decent shot but I''m not sure it demonstrates wind as effectively as it could.  The one candle that is not lit isn''t showing smouldering, and the flames on the others are not bent in a direction to suggest wind is blowing.  I do like the composition.</td>', 'Overall, this is a decent shot but I''m not sure it demonstrates wind as effectively as it could.  The one candle that is not lit isn''t showing smouldering, and the flames on the others are not bent in a direction to suggest wind is blowing.  I do like the composition.', '2004-12-05 13:10:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047087, 122389, 28261, '<td valign="top">Not much lower tech wake up device than this wonder.  Good lighting and long exposure of second hand and ringing bells.  No question that this is a loud subject!  Very clear focus and the noise in the shadows provides a graininess that I find interesting rather than detracting. Up angle gives it a larger than life feel that adds to the ''noise'' of the alarm.  Good Job, very high marks.</td>', 'Not much lower tech wake up device than this wonder.  Good lighting and long exposure of second hand and ringing bells.  No question that this is a loud subject!  Very clear focus and the noise in the shadows provides a graininess that I find interesting rather than detracting. Up angle gives it a larger than life feel that adds to the ''noise'' of the alarm.  Good Job, very high marks.', '2004-12-05 13:13:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047088, 124572, 29009, '<td valign="top">Excellent use of color here, and creative use of lines in the composition.  Good subject that meets the challenge.  If this had been in better focus I would have given it an extra point.</td>', 'Excellent use of color here, and creative use of lines in the composition.  Good subject that meets the challenge.  If this had been in better focus I would have given it an extra point.', '2004-12-05 13:14:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047091, 124319, 29009, '<td valign="top">Excellent!  Great subject, great focus, great artistic choice to use B&amp;W, great use of depth of field to make focal point pop.  Overall, a very strong image.</td>', 'Excellent!  Great subject, great focus, great artistic choice to use B&W, great use of depth of field to make focal point pop.  Overall, a very strong image.', '2004-12-05 13:15:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047095, 124280, 29009, '<td valign="top">You''ve got a solid idea here.  Unfortunately, the image as submitted is so small I''m afraid it might not do as well as it could.  Good use of depth of field.  Title distracts from overall shot as the teeth of the saw don''t appear to be in sharp focus, but this could be a result of the size of the submission.</td>', 'You''ve got a solid idea here.  Unfortunately, the image as submitted is so small I''m afraid it might not do as well as it could.  Good use of depth of field.  Title distracts from overall shot as the teeth of the saw don''t appear to be in sharp focus, but this could be a result of the size of the submission.', '2004-12-05 13:17:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047097, 124640, 28261, '<td valign="top">Interestingly enough, without the hands to define it as a watch, the technology of the subject becomes almost non-existant to me.  It now seems nothing more than a medal of honor, a trophy of some sort.  The blue above, only adding to that feeling.  I like the angle chosen to shoot from and chosen for teh subject itself, the DOF is great and keeps the whole in focus and the lighting allows it to gently melt into the background.  Overall a pleasant image, but distracting in the color above and lacking somehow in the tech arena but only because of the missing hands.  Desat the blue above tho and this image seems to me to be a winner for an abstract wallhanging.</td>', 'Interestingly enough, without the hands to define it as a watch, the technology of the subject becomes almost non-existant to me.  It now seems nothing more than a medal of honor, a trophy of some sort.  The blue above, only adding to that feeling.  I like the angle chosen to shoot from and chosen for teh subject itself, the DOF is great and keeps the whole in focus and the lighting allows it to gently melt into the background.  Overall a pleasant image, but distracting in the color above and lacking somehow in the tech arena but only because of the missing hands.  Desat the blue above tho and this image seems to me to be a winner for an abstract wallhanging.', '2004-12-05 13:18:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047100, 124464, 29009, '<td valign="top">Composition could be stronger to draw attention to the stone wall as a focal point.  This was an original idea.</td>', 'Composition could be stronger to draw attention to the stone wall as a focal point.  This was an original idea.', '2004-12-05 13:20:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047102, 122762, 28261, '<td valign="top">Black on Grey, lots of grey.  I see mchanics of some kind, but not technology per se.  The subject is overcome by the negative space, but not so overcome as to be overwhelmed and dwarfed by it which would be a statement.  Instead, it seems to have just less than 50% of the space in the frame and becomes a cacophany of lines against a grey palate.  Your focus is very good and the attempt to use thirds for composistion is a good effort that fails only due to the subject matter not having enough solid matter to overtake the power of the grey sky.</td>', 'Black on Grey, lots of grey.  I see mchanics of some kind, but not technology per se.  The subject is overcome by the negative space, but not so overcome as to be overwhelmed and dwarfed by it which would be a statement.  Instead, it seems to have just less than 50% of the space in the frame and becomes a cacophany of lines against a grey palate.  Your focus is very good and the attempt to use thirds for composistion is a good effort that fails only due to the subject matter not having enough solid matter to overtake the power of the grey sky.', '2004-12-05 13:22:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047105, 124371, 29009, '<td valign="top">Good composition and subject matter.  There is a distracting line at the back of the little boy''s neck that appears created by post-processing.  Otherwise, good use of selective saturation to bring attention to focal point.</td>', 'Good composition and subject matter.  There is a distracting line at the back of the little boy''s neck that appears created by post-processing.  Otherwise, good use of selective saturation to bring attention to focal point.', '2004-12-05 13:22:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047113, 122990, 29009, '<td valign="top">Good subject.  As is, the house competes with the pump for focal point attention.  Composition could have been improved by using a shorter depth of field - having the pump in sharper focus than the house in the background.  Alternately, a tighter crop on the pump would have also worked. Overall, a decent shot.</td>', 'Good subject.  As is, the house competes with the pump for focal point attention.  Composition could have been improved by using a shorter depth of field - having the pump in sharper focus than the house in the background.  Alternately, a tighter crop on the pump would have also worked. Overall, a decent shot.', '2004-12-05 13:26:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047125, 122250, 29009, '<td valign="top">This is truly a "WOW" shot and I hope it wins something.  Meets the challenge spot on.  Composition is excellent - subject has visual interest and it''s pretty perfect technically.  (10)</td>', 'This is truly a "WOW" shot and I hope it wins something.  Meets the challenge spot on.  Composition is excellent - subject has visual interest and it''s pretty perfect technically.  (10)', '2004-12-05 13:34:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047127, 124260, 29009, '<td valign="top">Excellent choice of subject.  Unfortunately, the image size is so small it is difficult to review for technical aspects.</td>', 'Excellent choice of subject.  Unfortunately, the image size is so small it is difficult to review for technical aspects.', '2004-12-05 13:35:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047134, 124586, 29009, '<td valign="top">Image size could have been bigger.  Unfortunately, your focal point is buried in leaves and I can''t identify it.</td>', 'Image size could have been bigger.  Unfortunately, your focal point is buried in leaves and I can''t identify it.', '2004-12-05 13:37:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047164, 124460, 28261, '<td valign="top">Definitely invokes a feeling of nostalgia and something of a low tech subject is captured in the popper.  The image elements are situated as to require the crop that has been chosen but the size of each subject and the enormous negative space detract considerably from the impact of the whole.   A tighter crop, larger elements and maybe fewer popcorn boxes would greatly improve this shot.</td>', 'Definitely invokes a feeling of nostalgia and something of a low tech subject is captured in the popper.  The image elements are situated as to require the crop that has been chosen but the size of each subject and the enormous negative space detract considerably from the impact of the whole.   A tighter crop, larger elements and maybe fewer popcorn boxes would greatly improve this shot.', '2004-12-05 13:58:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047179, 124189, 28261, '<td valign="top">Good use of shadows to enhance the focus of subject matter.  The candle seems to be less of the subject than the book and glasses however.  Nice balance of placements of the elements, but the left side of the book is distracting, makes me think that it is going to close on you.  Positioning the glasses across the binding may have been effective in thwarting that, but would have introduced a different crop or placement of elements that would defeat the shadowing.  I see the low tech element but it seems overwhelemed by the book as the focal point.  Nice subtle border and choice of accent color.</td>', 'Good use of shadows to enhance the focus of subject matter.  The candle seems to be less of the subject than the book and glasses however.  Nice balance of placements of the elements, but the left side of the book is distracting, makes me think that it is going to close on you.  Positioning the glasses across the binding may have been effective in thwarting that, but would have introduced a different crop or placement of elements that would defeat the shadowing.  I see the low tech element but it seems overwhelemed by the book as the focal point.  Nice subtle border and choice of accent color.', '2004-12-05 14:04:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047184, 123522, 28261, '<td valign="top">Selective desat worked well in this as my eyes can hardly move from the subject which is obviously low tech.  There is a shovel like formation just under the bulb of the pump that is distracting and should be cloned out.  I find the choice of DOF fine in this image and the trench/stream in teh background helps to keep a flow of the photo while subtly creating a division between foreground interests and background.  Nice!</td>', 'Selective desat worked well in this as my eyes can hardly move from the subject which is obviously low tech.  There is a shovel like formation just under the bulb of the pump that is distracting and should be cloned out.  I find the choice of DOF fine in this image and the trench/stream in teh background helps to keep a flow of the photo while subtly creating a division between foreground interests and background.  Nice!', '2004-12-05 14:08:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047192, 124198, 28261, '<td valign="top">Without the title, this image would not survive the challenge interpretation, but it is exactly worded to force me into that mind of thinking.  This is dustpan technology and as such, the low tech works.  The soft focus and highlights almost lend to an ethereal presentation that could be a marketing tool - the latest low tech wonder for the household.  Great job on interpretation and composition and leading title-generation.</td>', 'Without the title, this image would not survive the challenge interpretation, but it is exactly worded to force me into that mind of thinking.  This is dustpan technology and as such, the low tech works.  The soft focus and highlights almost lend to an ethereal presentation that could be a marketing tool - the latest low tech wonder for the household.  Great job on interpretation and composition and leading title-generation.', '2004-12-05 14:11:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047199, 123008, 28261, '<td valign="top">Another one who''s title solidly agrees with the subject and makes it impossible to think there is no technology involved.  It invokes the images of La Machine to compare it with.  I''m not so confident on the crop and placement of the eggplant?  A different angle on the chopper with more focus lent to the chopped green would have more impact, but it appears that the extras may have been needed to keep the subject from rolling away.  Nice shallow DOF keeps my eyes on the chopper blades, but it seems a bit off centered from where it should be.</td>', 'Another one who''s title solidly agrees with the subject and makes it impossible to think there is no technology involved.  It invokes the images of La Machine to compare it with.  I''m not so confident on the crop and placement of the eggplant?  A different angle on the chopper with more focus lent to the chopped green would have more impact, but it appears that the extras may have been needed to keep the subject from rolling away.  Nice shallow DOF keeps my eyes on the chopper blades, but it seems a bit off centered from where it should be.', '2004-12-05 14:16:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047203, 124967, 28261, '<td valign="top">I am impressed by the ''cleanness'' of this shot and the blurred action really adds to the interest level.  It is well balanced in the chosen crop and the lighting is not overdone in any part, but I am distracted by what appears to be the greyness of either dodging, desaturation or wrong light reflection in the upper right.  This seems way out of place with the rest of the image and has a strong negative impact on the whole.</td>', 'I am impressed by the ''cleanness'' of this shot and the blurred action really adds to the interest level.  It is well balanced in the chosen crop and the lighting is not overdone in any part, but I am distracted by what appears to be the greyness of either dodging, desaturation or wrong light reflection in the upper right.  This seems way out of place with the rest of the image and has a strong negative impact on the whole.', '2004-12-05 14:20:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047205, 123907, 28261, '<td valign="top">Yes, compared to an H, O or HO scale toy, better believe its low tech.  Cropped a bit tight on the sides, some more white (not much mind you) would really make this stand out.  Lighting on the flat foreface is perfect, but on the platform and upper section seems way overdone, perhaps moving the backlight away more or dropping its power a stop or two would provide a more even feel.  Seems to be a bunch of dust on the platform as well.  I hate dusting, but I think it would go a long way to giving the shot an extra edge.</td>', 'Yes, compared to an H, O or HO scale toy, better believe its low tech.  Cropped a bit tight on the sides, some more white (not much mind you) would really make this stand out.  Lighting on the flat foreface is perfect, but on the platform and upper section seems way overdone, perhaps moving the backlight away more or dropping its power a stop or two would provide a more even feel.  Seems to be a bunch of dust on the platform as well.  I hate dusting, but I think it would go a long way to giving the shot an extra edge.', '2004-12-05 14:24:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047207, 124167, 28261, '<td valign="top">Technologically low - Yes.  Non-Electronic - Nope.  Nostalgic - beyond a shadow of a doubt.  I like the diagonal centralized lighting on this piece the angle of presentation, patterns, textures and perhaps even the dust or grain resulting around the push buttons.  The text is easy to see, this is a great antique-style foto getting high marks, but has serious loss in the application of low-tech use no electronics.</td>', 'Technologically low - Yes.  Non-Electronic - Nope.  Nostalgic - beyond a shadow of a doubt.  I like the diagonal centralized lighting on this piece the angle of presentation, patterns, textures and perhaps even the dust or grain resulting around the push buttons.  The text is easy to see, this is a great antique-style foto getting high marks, but has serious loss in the application of low-tech use no electronics.', '2004-12-05 14:28:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047210, 124363, 28261, '<td valign="top">Very colorful shot, nice contrast with the wood grain and the background even lends to the interest level.  All the elements seem to be in just the right focus.  Disappointed in the top area of the crop as there seems to be an uneven distribution of the negative space up there.  Perhaps if the tomato was ''lowered'' on the stage and the upper corner of the cutting board were also cropped, this would improve.  The knife blade seems dull compared to the rest of the shot and may have more impact if it were a wider blade.  Overall tho I have to give some high marks for this as it has an eye-candy feel to it that is very appealing.</td>', 'Very colorful shot, nice contrast with the wood grain and the background even lends to the interest level.  All the elements seem to be in just the right focus.  Disappointed in the top area of the crop as there seems to be an uneven distribution of the negative space up there.  Perhaps if the tomato was ''lowered'' on the stage and the upper corner of the cutting board were also cropped, this would improve.  The knife blade seems dull compared to the rest of the shot and may have more impact if it were a wider blade.  Overall tho I have to give some high marks for this as it has an eye-candy feel to it that is very appealing.', '2004-12-05 14:34:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047214, 122776, 28261, '<td valign="top">I''m having a hard time with the leap from weatervane to technology although I recogize that we now have weather stations that are very high tech.  It''s intepretive artistically.  The most distracting element of this image is the reversed N-S.  Admittedly, this is a result of wind, but it takes away from an otherwise well presented and cropped image with solid contrast and coloring.</td>', 'I''m having a hard time with the leap from weatervane to technology although I recogize that we now have weather stations that are very high tech.  It''s intepretive artistically.  The most distracting element of this image is the reversed N-S.  Admittedly, this is a result of wind, but it takes away from an otherwise well presented and cropped image with solid contrast and coloring.', '2004-12-05 14:37:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047218, 124369, 28261, '<td valign="top">Recognizing that some games are now electronic or even video, I have to say that the subject does not really say low tech to me.  This is a nice ''stock'' presentation of a board game, a lttile soft on the edges, and has some over exposure on the top flat areas.  An interesting presentation despite these notes, the color use is inviting, but overall seems to need corrections to those items to really hold the attention of the viewer.</td>', 'Recognizing that some games are now electronic or even video, I have to say that the subject does not really say low tech to me.  This is a nice ''stock'' presentation of a board game, a lttile soft on the edges, and has some over exposure on the top flat areas.  An interesting presentation despite these notes, the color use is inviting, but overall seems to need corrections to those items to really hold the attention of the viewer.', '2004-12-05 14:41:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047222, 124972, 28261, '<td valign="top">Great use of a wide, clean blade to create the reflections, color on the green pepper seems a bit desaturated or flat, the red pepper really sticks out and the action of cutting gives this a nice feel.  The negative space at the top detracts from the whole, either more peppers are needed in that space to keep the aspect ration of the desired print or the crop should be shortened at the top to emphasize the focus of the blade in action.</td>', 'Great use of a wide, clean blade to create the reflections, color on the green pepper seems a bit desaturated or flat, the red pepper really sticks out and the action of cutting gives this a nice feel.  The negative space at the top detracts from the whole, either more peppers are needed in that space to keep the aspect ration of the desired print or the crop should be shortened at the top to emphasize the focus of the blade in action.', '2004-12-05 14:44:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047223, 122267, 28261, '<td valign="top">Nicely framed subject, obviously low tech, well cropped and draws me to looking right at the subject.  Had to work, just to view the surrounding environ and that is good.  The chain pattern on the barrel is hypnotic if you stare at it (Moire?) but not distracting except that I chose to concentrate on it.  use of black and white and the resulting border put some great finishing touches on this shot.  Nice job!</td>', 'Nicely framed subject, obviously low tech, well cropped and draws me to looking right at the subject.  Had to work, just to view the surrounding environ and that is good.  The chain pattern on the barrel is hypnotic if you stare at it (Moire?) but not distracting except that I chose to concentrate on it.  use of black and white and the resulting border put some great finishing touches on this shot.  Nice job!', '2004-12-05 14:50:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047224, 124502, 28261, '<td valign="top">Not much lower tech than this.  I picture the unfortunate slaves pushing one of these around in those movies and it invokes the lowest of tech, human powered.  Contrasts are great here, the powdery highlights and sooty shadows of age.  I feel cramped in the space here which only lends to the feel of an oppressively unperfected mode of doing things.  Good job, High marks all around.</td>', 'Not much lower tech than this.  I picture the unfortunate slaves pushing one of these around in those movies and it invokes the lowest of tech, human powered.  Contrasts are great here, the powdery highlights and sooty shadows of age.  I feel cramped in the space here which only lends to the feel of an oppressively unperfected mode of doing things.  Good job, High marks all around.', '2004-12-05 14:53:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047227, 123717, 28261, '<td valign="top">Well framed nice color and an obviously low tech answer to food processing.  The angle adds a lot to the interest level as does the handle position and the plaster wall''s stark bleach color.  Only obvious thing I see that could improve this might be the punch of a contrast boost from the unsharp mask (%:20, rad: 50-100, levels:0).  Perhaps too the back apple is not red enough for the rest of the shot.  Great image.</td>', 'Well framed nice color and an obviously low tech answer to food processing.  The angle adds a lot to the interest level as does the handle position and the plaster wall''s stark bleach color.  Only obvious thing I see that could improve this might be the punch of a contrast boost from the unsharp mask (%:20, rad: 50-100, levels:0).  Perhaps too the back apple is not red enough for the rest of the shot.  Great image.', '2004-12-05 14:57:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047259, 122990, 22781, '<td valign="top">Oh, so that are waterpumps?<br/>I see them all the time in American films (movies whatever word you like) normaly they are broken and make a sqeeky sound :-) But now I know what they are..<br/>I learn every day... If you know how they work you can tell mee because I dont see anything go into the ground...<br/> <br/>On the photo, it''s 100% low-tech and the nice house and the sky add to the photo.. (8)</td>', 'Oh, so that are waterpumps?I see them all the time in American films (movies whatever word you like) normaly they are broken and make a sqeeky sound :-) But now I know what they are..I learn every day... If you know how they work you can tell mee because I dont see anything go into the ground... On the photo, it''s 100% low-tech and the nice house and the sky add to the photo.. (8)', '2004-12-05 16:05:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047260, 124545, 22781, '<td valign="top">You know that I have repaird these kind of camera''s? Fun isn''t it?<br/>Good luck!</td>', 'You know that I have repaird these kind of camera''s? Fun isn''t it?Good luck!', '2004-12-05 16:06:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047267, 124502, 27847, '<td valign="top">Really nice picture on this wheels, interesting too. I haven''t seen one of these in a very long time. The only thing that looks funny is the blue color in the shot, almost as if the wrong white balance setting was set on the camera!?! Still really nice compisition.</td>', 'Really nice picture on this wheels, interesting too. I haven''t seen one of these in a very long time. The only thing that looks funny is the blue color in the shot, almost as if the wrong white balance setting was set on the camera!?! Still really nice compisition.', '2004-12-05 16:12:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047268, 124493, 27847, '<td valign="top">Love what you have done with the photo here, almost makes it look like it was taken in 1916. Great Job.</td>', 'Love what you have done with the photo here, almost makes it look like it was taken in 1916. Great Job.', '2004-12-05 16:13:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047271, 124623, 27847, '<td valign="top">Hey, I wouldn''t be using that opener, looks a little rusty ;-) Great shot, love the lighting on this shot. Only thing I would change is the label, I have a feeling it might have looked a little better without the Beef label. Still, excellent work.</td>', 'Hey, I wouldn''t be using that opener, looks a little rusty ;-) Great shot, love the lighting on this shot. Only thing I would change is the label, I have a feeling it might have looked a little better without the Beef label. Still, excellent work.', '2004-12-05 16:19:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047273, 124394, 27847, '<td valign="top">Wow, these things still exist? This show would have worked great with some low depth of field.</td>', 'Wow, these things still exist? This show would have worked great with some low depth of field.', '2004-12-05 16:23:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047275, 124260, 27847, '<td valign="top">Great idea for a low tech device however, his might have had more impact if it was a whole shot of the flour shifter. If anything this shot needs to be a lot larger. Very tiny photo.</td>', 'Great idea for a low tech device however, his might have had more impact if it was a whole shot of the flour shifter. If anything this shot needs to be a lot larger. Very tiny photo.', '2004-12-05 16:27:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047277, 124967, 27847, '<td valign="top">High marks, love this shot. Great example of low tech device from the old days. The lighting and the composition is superb. Excellent work.</td>', 'High marks, love this shot. Great example of low tech device from the old days. The lighting and the composition is superb. Excellent work.', '2004-12-05 16:30:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047287, 123451, 3032, '<td valign="top">I just love this photo, the whole setup looks so classic.  The B*W toning, the pushed-like exposure and good old film like grain is just great. I also think that it has a pretty strong composition with the lights guiding the viewer trough the frame, the view into the depth and some people in it to be able to judge sizes.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I just love this photo, the whole setup looks so classic.  The B*W toning, the pushed-like exposure and good old film like grain is just great. I also think that it has a pretty strong composition with the lights guiding the viewer trough the frame, the view into the depth and some people in it to be able to judge sizes. ', '2004-12-05 16:47:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047291, 122432, 3032, '<td valign="top">I did something like this a year (or two) ago witg my old socks, but this is far better.<br/>Strong composition, color and contrast. Nice DOF, good bokeh. Like it.</td>', 'I did something like this a year (or two) ago witg my old socks, but this is far better.Strong composition, color and contrast. Nice DOF, good bokeh. Like it.', '2004-12-05 16:50:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047292, 124751, 3032, '<td valign="top">Pastel-like soft colors, good lighting and interesting because of the way it shows movement.  Nice work.<br/></td>', 'Pastel-like soft colors, good lighting and interesting because of the way it shows movement.  Nice work.', '2004-12-05 16:51:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047297, 123357, 3032, '<td valign="top">Well, it still lacks a needle or you must have some magic trick to attatch those buttons to a fabric with that wire. :)<br/> <br/>Overall great lighting but the shadow is a bit dark. A reflector opposite the light source may help to fill and soften it a bit. I''ve used whire cardboard, A4 white printing paper, wrinkled alu foil myself. Composition is good, but might look stronger in a 3:2 ratio. I say that because the left and right side are so close to the subjects that you''d expect a bit less space on top and at the bottom. 7</td>', 'Well, it still lacks a needle or you must have some magic trick to attatch those buttons to a fabric with that wire. :) Overall great lighting but the shadow is a bit dark. A reflector opposite the light source may help to fill and soften it a bit. I''ve used whire cardboard, A4 white printing paper, wrinkled alu foil myself. Composition is good, but might look stronger in a 3:2 ratio. I say that because the left and right side are so close to the subjects that you''d expect a bit less space on top and at the bottom. 7', '2004-12-05 16:56:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047302, 124883, 3032, '<td valign="top">A bit soft, but it makes the scene and colors flow very nicely. Air becomes water becomes land becomes manmade object. The colors goe from deep blue to light yellow-orange in a very nice way.<br/>The composition is nice but I guess that the scene lends itself for a nice and wide panorama (the lighthouse is relatively close to the side of the frame), something dpc is not yet well suited for. :( I like it how the rocks and land lead the viewer to the tower from the left to the right. The light in the lighthouse finishes it off. Is that the lighthouse its own light or a reflection from the sun in one of the mirrors? 7</td>', 'A bit soft, but it makes the scene and colors flow very nicely. Air becomes water becomes land becomes manmade object. The colors goe from deep blue to light yellow-orange in a very nice way.The composition is nice but I guess that the scene lends itself for a nice and wide panorama (the lighthouse is relatively close to the side of the frame), something dpc is not yet well suited for. :( I like it how the rocks and land lead the viewer to the tower from the left to the right. The light in the lighthouse finishes it off. Is that the lighthouse its own light or a reflection from the sun in one of the mirrors? 7', '2004-12-05 17:00:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047304, 124167, 3032, '<td valign="top">I really like the lighting with the emphasize on the wavelengths here. The color and toning makes it look really classic, the subject deserves it.</td>', 'I really like the lighting with the emphasize on the wavelengths here. The color and toning makes it look really classic, the subject deserves it.', '2004-12-05 17:02:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047308, 124697, 3032, '<td valign="top">The tractor (do I use the right word?) makes this picture work for me. Because it provides such dark contrast against the other parts of the scene.<br/>To improve I''d suggest to straighten the horizon. The roof of the house provides a good line for that. The background is a bit bright in relation to the foreground and that draws the attention away a bit. Could be imroved by some burning.<br/>The pattern of the hills looks familiar (only seen it once), California?<br/> <br/></td>', 'The tractor (do I use the right word?) makes this picture work for me. Because it provides such dark contrast against the other parts of the scene.To improve I''d suggest to straighten the horizon. The roof of the house provides a good line for that. The background is a bit bright in relation to the foreground and that draws the attention away a bit. Could be imroved by some burning.The pattern of the hills looks familiar (only seen it once), California? ', '2004-12-05 17:06:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047316, 122250, 3032, '<td valign="top">Conditions like mist are great to photograph historical subjects without the modern stuff like 20th century buildings, cars and IJ-tunnels in the background.  It is one of the things that bugs me the most when I visit historical sites, always those damn cars and mopeds. :(<br/>A bit unortunate that they had those non-sailing-related-sails on the side of the ship, I guess they were painting. I am already looking forward to SAIL Amsterdam 2005 btw.<br/> <br/>Anyway, about the photo:<br/>I like the portrayal here, with the emphasize on the interesting rear section and the classic curved line towards the front, somewhat disappearing into the mist. Colors are pretty good as well as the exposure. Stuff like that can be pretty hard in the flat mist light.<br/>The horizon on the left looks a bit unnatural (cloning, gaussian blur?), but it is not that distracting.<br/> <br/>Nice work.</td>', 'Conditions like mist are great to photograph historical subjects without the modern stuff like 20th century buildings, cars and IJ-tunnels in the background.  It is one of the things that bugs me the most when I visit historical sites, always those damn cars and mopeds. :(A bit unortunate that they had those non-sailing-related-sails on the side of the ship, I guess they were painting. I am already looking forward to SAIL Amsterdam 2005 btw. Anyway, about the photo:I like the portrayal here, with the emphasize on the interesting rear section and the classic curved line towards the front, somewhat disappearing into the mist. Colors are pretty good as well as the exposure. Stuff like that can be pretty hard in the flat mist light.The horizon on the left looks a bit unnatural (cloning, gaussian blur?), but it is not that distracting. Nice work.', '2004-12-05 17:14:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047321, 122990, 3032, '<td valign="top">The water pump is very interesting, especially because of the beautiful rotor, but the house draws to much attention away imho. Perhaps that another angle or just using the rotor itself as a subject might create a stronger impact. The way the light from the back illuminates the rotor blades from the back is interesting. Despite that the composition is good.<br/>Exposure and contrast balance is very good, colors look natural.</td>', 'The water pump is very interesting, especially because of the beautiful rotor, but the house draws to much attention away imho. Perhaps that another angle or just using the rotor itself as a subject might create a stronger impact. The way the light from the back illuminates the rotor blades from the back is interesting. Despite that the composition is good.Exposure and contrast balance is very good, colors look natural.', '2004-12-05 17:20:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047328, 124115, 3032, '<td valign="top">The flames always burn out so easily, this one is just about right. The illumination of the hands is just great, good exposure, nice warm color.<br/></td>', 'The flames always burn out so easily, this one is just about right. The illumination of the hands is just great, good exposure, nice warm color.', '2004-12-05 17:30:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047339, 124863, 28261, '<td valign="top">Solidly low tech, not much lower: easy comparison to modern vehicles.  The contrast seems a bit washed out or maybe it''s hazy. (Could be fixed with unsharp trick#226 - %=20-40, radius=50-200, levels=0).</td>', 'Solidly low tech, not much lower: easy comparison to modern vehicles.  The contrast seems a bit washed out or maybe it''s hazy. (Could be fixed with unsharp trick#226 - %=20-40, radius=50-200, levels=0).', '2004-12-05 17:40:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047342, 124863, 3032, '<td valign="top">The composition is pretty good with the position of the ''buggy'' and the way the fence and road lead out of the frame. The overal scene seems like it is brightened a bit or the exposure is a bit flat. Let me load it in Photoshop.......<br/> <br/>The histogram shows that most exposure values lay in the middle, the scene has only 3 stops worth of information. By adjusting the levels you can stretch it out to five to get a better distribution. Load it into your favorite post-processing software (as long as it has levels adjustments). Now change the input values to 23 (from 0) for the left slider and 209 (from 255) for the right slider. This is just a base setting, try to experiment to get to the best settings. A levels adjustment can improve the contrast of this shot quite a bit.<br/> <br/></td>', 'The composition is pretty good with the position of the ''buggy'' and the way the fence and road lead out of the frame. The overal scene seems like it is brightened a bit or the exposure is a bit flat. Let me load it in Photoshop....... The histogram shows that most exposure values lay in the middle, the scene has only 3 stops worth of information. By adjusting the levels you can stretch it out to five to get a better distribution. Load it into your favorite post-processing software (as long as it has levels adjustments). Now change the input values to 23 (from 0) for the left slider and 209 (from 255) for the right slider. This is just a base setting, try to experiment to get to the best settings. A levels adjustment can improve the contrast of this shot quite a bit. ', '2004-12-05 17:42:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047349, 123713, 28261, '<td valign="top">A great photo, but nowhere on the low tech range.  The comparison of this guitar, to another would mean comparing to an acoustic.  Framing is good, bit of noise in the red shadows, blur of hand is just right and not distracting. DOF seems very good for the presentation.  High marks on composition, big hit for challenge details.</td>', 'A great photo, but nowhere on the low tech range.  The comparison of this guitar, to another would mean comparing to an acoustic.  Framing is good, bit of noise in the red shadows, blur of hand is just right and not distracting. DOF seems very good for the presentation.  High marks on composition, big hit for challenge details.', '2004-12-05 17:48:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047408, 122432, 8054, '<td valign="top">Nice sharp contrast and creative way to use the "handle" of the clothes pin to lead the eyes to the spring. I might have placed the "handles" a bit higher (or lower) so the spring rests on a 1/3 mark both horizontally and vertically.</td>', 'Nice sharp contrast and creative way to use the "handle" of the clothes pin to lead the eyes to the spring. I might have placed the "handles" a bit higher (or lower) so the spring rests on a 1/3 mark both horizontally and vertically.', '2004-12-05 18:24:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047411, 124202, 8054, '<td valign="top">I think this was oversharpened as many lines are overemphasized and jaggy.</td>', 'I think this was oversharpened as many lines are overemphasized and jaggy.', '2004-12-05 18:25:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047432, 121877, 28261, '<td valign="top">Great example of low tech, in fact a throw back to teh stone age! Nice interesting textures and placement of the elements.  Very distracting dodge remnants on the sides of the pestle creating a hazy glow from behind and below.  A careful use of the history brush in adv editing would easily clean this up and leave a near perfect image.</td>', 'Great example of low tech, in fact a throw back to teh stone age! Nice interesting textures and placement of the elements.  Very distracting dodge remnants on the sides of the pestle creating a hazy glow from behind and below.  A careful use of the history brush in adv editing would easily clean this up and leave a near perfect image.', '2004-12-05 18:52:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047436, 121763, 28261, '<td valign="top">Certainly low tech.  Somewhat electronic, but might pass as non.  Love the way the camera''s positional angle points to the lens, but then the lens is defocused forcing the viewer to revisit the camera as the subject.  This might be considered distracting, I find it innovatively artistic.  Nice choice of crop and frame size.</td>', 'Certainly low tech.  Somewhat electronic, but might pass as non.  Love the way the camera''s positional angle points to the lens, but then the lens is defocused forcing the viewer to revisit the camera as the subject.  This might be considered distracting, I find it innovatively artistic.  Nice choice of crop and frame size.', '2004-12-05 18:55:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047437, 123732, 28261, '<td valign="top">Definitely low tech.  Something about your camera angle makes this look like the egg beater is hanging in mid air with a table above it (rotated 180 degrees perhaps?)  The highlight on the end of the beater seems overdone, but achieves a side-effect of drawing my eye right to that focal point.   A second light on the top left corner would balance the whole and make the subject look less suspended.  Nice detail on the subject itself however.</td>', 'Definitely low tech.  Something about your camera angle makes this look like the egg beater is hanging in mid air with a table above it (rotated 180 degrees perhaps?)  The highlight on the end of the beater seems overdone, but achieves a side-effect of drawing my eye right to that focal point.   A second light on the top left corner would balance the whole and make the subject look less suspended.  Nice detail on the subject itself however.', '2004-12-05 18:59:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047442, 124973, 28261, '<td valign="top">Tape technology.  I am challenged to see technology in tape (compared to other fasterners?  compared to other tape?)  In some ways it could be argued that duct tape is high tech compared to scotch.  The subject is well placed in the frame and falls out of the frame at a good locations as well.  DOF just enough to make what is important stay in focus and what is secondary becomes an afterthought.  Little strong on the highlight over the single tape but causes a blending into the background that works for the whole.  Overall good composition, feel I''m stretching too much for technology, but the idea sticks well anyway.</td>', 'Tape technology.  I am challenged to see technology in tape (compared to other fasterners?  compared to other tape?)  In some ways it could be argued that duct tape is high tech compared to scotch.  The subject is well placed in the frame and falls out of the frame at a good locations as well.  DOF just enough to make what is important stay in focus and what is secondary becomes an afterthought.  Little strong on the highlight over the single tape but causes a blending into the background that works for the whole.  Overall good composition, feel I''m stretching too much for technology, but the idea sticks well anyway.', '2004-12-05 19:04:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047446, 123688, 28261, '<td valign="top">Great example of low tech.  Like the addition of currencies and beans and the choice of background color is a perfect offset to the abacus itself.  The texture of the table adds a subtle grain that adds quite a bit of interest to the whole and the angle chosen with crop makes for a very solid contender.</td>', 'Great example of low tech.  Like the addition of currencies and beans and the choice of background color is a perfect offset to the abacus itself.  The texture of the table adds a subtle grain that adds quite a bit of interest to the whole and the angle chosen with crop makes for a very solid contender.', '2004-12-05 19:06:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047449, 124942, 28261, '<td valign="top">Definitely low tech transport.  Your choice of a bleaching in b/w has a positive effect on aging the image even more.  It is well placed and cropped, perhaps slightly too much on the top, but this is not detracting in any way. Nice job!</td>', 'Definitely low tech transport.  Your choice of a bleaching in b/w has a positive effect on aging the image even more.  It is well placed and cropped, perhaps slightly too much on the top, but this is not detracting in any way. Nice job!', '2004-12-05 19:09:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047452, 123481, 12573, '<td valign="top">This is sort of a bizarre photograph (not that that''s always a bad thing).  I''m guessing the elephant was carved out of wood, but one can only guess given that the sculpture is out of focus.  The suspended nature of the chisel is weird.  It''s kinda twilight zone-ish, which isnt very appropriate given the subject.  The shadow of the chisel on the back wall is distracting to me.  I really don''t know what to tell you to do to improve the photo.  Perhaps recompose with a sculpture that is clearly made of wood...maybe partly completed.  Also, I would take a more downward angle toward the subject.  This sort of subject usually looks best when taken at a natural point of view, as from the eye of the woodworker.</td>', 'This is sort of a bizarre photograph (not that that''s always a bad thing).  I''m guessing the elephant was carved out of wood, but one can only guess given that the sculpture is out of focus.  The suspended nature of the chisel is weird.  It''s kinda twilight zone-ish, which isnt very appropriate given the subject.  The shadow of the chisel on the back wall is distracting to me.  I really don''t know what to tell you to do to improve the photo.  Perhaps recompose with a sculpture that is clearly made of wood...maybe partly completed.  Also, I would take a more downward angle toward the subject.  This sort of subject usually looks best when taken at a natural point of view, as from the eye of the woodworker.', '2004-12-05 19:12:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047456, 122600, 28261, '<td valign="top">I am struck first with the choice of subject, the horse or the tools, as I consider these, I note that the rope above the horse''s ear appears like a noose almost holding up the horse''s head.  This has become too distracting to me.  I like the choice of desaturation and color cast as it ages the image.  The varied elements are in good focus or shadowed well in their own place, but the elements vying for my attention challenge the whole as separate things that dont want to add up.</td>', 'I am struck first with the choice of subject, the horse or the tools, as I consider these, I note that the rope above the horse''s ear appears like a noose almost holding up the horse''s head.  This has become too distracting to me.  I like the choice of desaturation and color cast as it ages the image.  The varied elements are in good focus or shadowed well in their own place, but the elements vying for my attention challenge the whole as separate things that dont want to add up.', '2004-12-05 19:13:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047463, 122161, 28261, '<td valign="top">I am struck by the golden hue of this image.  At first glance it is powerful almost majestic, then my eye is drawn away by the flame and it''s reflection off the glass.  The brushed metal is well defined, lit and focused, but just below, the platform or support seems very out of place and the backlighting has cast shadows in the foreground supports that detract from the whole.  A slightly tigher crop, less backlight and a small amount more of foreground lighting would bring it all into balance.  I find the DOF very solid and the focus on the sandcatch excellent.  There is no doubt that this is a low tech item.</td>', 'I am struck by the golden hue of this image.  At first glance it is powerful almost majestic, then my eye is drawn away by the flame and it''s reflection off the glass.  The brushed metal is well defined, lit and focused, but just below, the platform or support seems very out of place and the backlighting has cast shadows in the foreground supports that detract from the whole.  A slightly tigher crop, less backlight and a small amount more of foreground lighting would bring it all into balance.  I find the DOF very solid and the focus on the sandcatch excellent.  There is no doubt that this is a low tech item.', '2004-12-05 19:21:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047467, 124931, 12573, '<td valign="top">You''ll likely be voted down for not really having a low tech subject, but I agree with you.  This is indeed on the verge of being considered low technology.  Still, the idea of reading magnetic tape that can be rewritten over and over might be disputable as a low tech medium.  Regardless of all that, you''ve got a nice composition with decent lighting (I like backlit subjects :).  Perhaps a little bounced fill lighting to further flesh some of the details in the front of the tape.  But leave the back light alone, it''s good.  Just bounce some into the front next time.  The depth of field is perfect given the size of the subject.  Dare I say you were perhaps too close to the subject?  Maybe about 1 inch further away would''ve given me a little more of the scene (tape rolls, background) to ponder.  Overall, a nice effort. 6.</td>', 'You''ll likely be voted down for not really having a low tech subject, but I agree with you.  This is indeed on the verge of being considered low technology.  Still, the idea of reading magnetic tape that can be rewritten over and over might be disputable as a low tech medium.  Regardless of all that, you''ve got a nice composition with decent lighting (I like backlit subjects :).  Perhaps a little bounced fill lighting to further flesh some of the details in the front of the tape.  But leave the back light alone, it''s good.  Just bounce some into the front next time.  The depth of field is perfect given the size of the subject.  Dare I say you were perhaps too close to the subject?  Maybe about 1 inch further away would''ve given me a little more of the scene (tape rolls, background) to ponder.  Overall, a nice effort. 6.', '2004-12-05 19:23:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047472, 123029, 28261, '<td valign="top">God this is a great collage!  I am torn: knowing that digital is the higher tech and film the lower tech and yet technology seems more ''gadgety'' to me.  Cannot fault on subject matter.  The artist here has evoked lower technology and done so in the most devious of ways.  I love the dof, fades on the corners and full background, excellent sharpness on the canister and central environment.  A cacophany of tiny different textures that all blend into a whole that draws the piece together.  Very nicely done.</td>', 'God this is a great collage!  I am torn: knowing that digital is the higher tech and film the lower tech and yet technology seems more ''gadgety'' to me.  Cannot fault on subject matter.  The artist here has evoked lower technology and done so in the most devious of ways.  I love the dof, fades on the corners and full background, excellent sharpness on the canister and central environment.  A cacophany of tiny different textures that all blend into a whole that draws the piece together.  Very nicely done.', '2004-12-05 19:26:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047473, 122990, 12573, '<td valign="top">That is perhaps the queerest looking windmill I''ve ever seen (so many blades!).  I think the inclusion of the house in the background is lovely and suits the windmill nicely.  I wonder if you''d have use a wider angle and gotten slightly closer to the windmill would that have been better.  Perhaps with a wider aperature as well to blur out the house, which would still be discernible.  I think the trees on the left could have been cropped out to better effect.  It''s definitely low tech, and you get a bonus for meeting the challenge.</td>', 'That is perhaps the queerest looking windmill I''ve ever seen (so many blades!).  I think the inclusion of the house in the background is lovely and suits the windmill nicely.  I wonder if you''d have use a wider angle and gotten slightly closer to the windmill would that have been better.  Perhaps with a wider aperature as well to blur out the house, which would still be discernible.  I think the trees on the left could have been cropped out to better effect.  It''s definitely low tech, and you get a bonus for meeting the challenge.', '2004-12-05 19:26:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047475, 122656, 12573, '<td valign="top">Wow, very nice and moody shot.  Does her hair on the left really offer anything to the composition?  I might have pulled it out of the way fo r the shot.  The position of the flute (?) is great and very comfortable to my eye.  I''m impressed that her ring is the same silver tone as the instrument.  If it were gold, it would be distracting.  Perhaps a good tip to others shooting musicians.  Match your jewelry! :) 9</td>', 'Wow, very nice and moody shot.  Does her hair on the left really offer anything to the composition?  I might have pulled it out of the way fo r the shot.  The position of the flute (?) is great and very comfortable to my eye.  I''m impressed that her ring is the same silver tone as the instrument.  If it were gold, it would be distracting.  Perhaps a good tip to others shooting musicians.  Match your jewelry! :) 9', '2004-12-05 19:28:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047478, 123906, 28261, '<td valign="top">Unwittingly or knowingly capturing two low tech items.  Antenna reception and wood heat.  The smoke does well to balance the antenna while the inclusion of the top corner of the roof gives a solid base to the image.  The smoke appears haloed by a lens flare or post process effect.  A little on the dark side in the brick and somewhat oversharpened or exposed on the antenna,.  A simple, easy to translate, low tech presentation.</td>', 'Unwittingly or knowingly capturing two low tech items.  Antenna reception and wood heat.  The smoke does well to balance the antenna while the inclusion of the top corner of the roof gives a solid base to the image.  The smoke appears haloed by a lens flare or post process effect.  A little on the dark side in the brick and somewhat oversharpened or exposed on the antenna,.  A simple, easy to translate, low tech presentation.', '2004-12-05 19:30:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047484, 124763, 28261, '<td valign="top">At first glance seems ordinary, but then finds balance in the shell coloring and the background cast, well sectioned off by the placement of the wisk and the backlit shadow.  Good DOF and focus, distracting highlight on the bottom egg on left, nice flow of shapes with ovals contrasted with the sharp angles.  I did not find myself thinking of low tech, but see that it very much is.</td>', 'At first glance seems ordinary, but then finds balance in the shell coloring and the background cast, well sectioned off by the placement of the wisk and the backlit shadow.  Good DOF and focus, distracting highlight on the bottom egg on left, nice flow of shapes with ovals contrasted with the sharp angles.  I did not find myself thinking of low tech, but see that it very much is.', '2004-12-05 19:34:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047485, 124603, 9780, '<td valign="top">Lik the collores in the background. nice cropping. 9+</td>', 'Lik the collores in the background. nice cropping. 9+', '2004-12-05 19:35:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047486, 124983, 12573, '<td valign="top">Very cool, nostalgic photo.  I wonder though if it''s immediately recognizable as a telephone.  I think having the handset a little more pronounced could have improved the shot.  The use of a high ISO or added grain in post-processing is flawless--I love it.   The lighting is fairly good, with a little too much light on the right and not enough on the left.  But not really bad.  I give it an 8.  Great stuff.</td>', 'Very cool, nostalgic photo.  I wonder though if it''s immediately recognizable as a telephone.  I think having the handset a little more pronounced could have improved the shot.  The use of a high ISO or added grain in post-processing is flawless--I love it.   The lighting is fairly good, with a little too much light on the right and not enough on the left.  But not really bad.  I give it an 8.  Great stuff.', '2004-12-05 19:35:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047489, 122505, 9780, '<td valign="top">Losing the handle of the shofel hurt this pic in my opinon. nice collor treatment, it makes the pic look old.8</td>', 'Losing the handle of the shofel hurt this pic in my opinon. nice collor treatment, it makes the pic look old.8', '2004-12-05 19:38:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047490, 124865, 12573, '<td valign="top">Very nice, soft-lighted still life of the nuts.  The placement of the nuts in front of the cracker seems a bit contrived.  Also, it doesn''t make a lot of sense that the bucket is full of unshelled nuts.  Isn''t the purpose of the bucket to catch the crushed shells?  Your positioning of the subject in the frame needs a little attention: if this were shot vertically, I think you could''ve gotten all of the nutcracker and the nuts in the shot without cutting the nuts off (ouch).  Overall, though the problems with the image are fairly petty. 7.</td>', 'Very nice, soft-lighted still life of the nuts.  The placement of the nuts in front of the cracker seems a bit contrived.  Also, it doesn''t make a lot of sense that the bucket is full of unshelled nuts.  Isn''t the purpose of the bucket to catch the crushed shells?  Your positioning of the subject in the frame needs a little attention: if this were shot vertically, I think you could''ve gotten all of the nutcracker and the nuts in the shot without cutting the nuts off (ouch).  Overall, though the problems with the image are fairly petty. 7.', '2004-12-05 19:39:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047493, 124292, 9780, '<td valign="top">maybe little light in backround would help this pic.</td>', 'maybe little light in backround would help this pic.', '2004-12-05 19:40:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047495, 124671, 9780, '<td valign="top">Nice view point. Good collor in the sky. Plain pic.</td>', 'Nice view point. Good collor in the sky. Plain pic.', '2004-12-05 19:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047496, 124906, 12573, '<td valign="top">Aww, reminds me of my youth.  I think you overexposed by about 1.5 stops.  I know that would darkened the blue piece too much, but the yellow piece is suffering from blown highlights.  The 1:1 (or close to it) aspect ratio isn''t really doing much for me, but I''m biased toward vertical portrait orientation in 4:3 ratio.  The lighting is superb.  The shadows are cast beautifully and seem very appropriate for the subject.  I really do like this though and I seem to be nitpicking. 8.</td>', 'Aww, reminds me of my youth.  I think you overexposed by about 1.5 stops.  I know that would darkened the blue piece too much, but the yellow piece is suffering from blown highlights.  The 1:1 (or close to it) aspect ratio isn''t really doing much for me, but I''m biased toward vertical portrait orientation in 4:3 ratio.  The lighting is superb.  The shadows are cast beautifully and seem very appropriate for the subject.  I really do like this though and I seem to be nitpicking. 8.', '2004-12-05 19:42:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047502, 122432, 9780, '<td valign="top">Nice one. baybe tan brighter? :) 9+</td>', 'Nice one. baybe tan brighter? :) 9+', '2004-12-05 19:44:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047503, 124967, 12573, '<td valign="top">Wow, this is just phenomenal work.  The motion capture is really good and the lighting, well, it''s perfect.  The texture on the platform is very important and helps my eye avoid seeing the spinning wheel as floating in midair.  Very good stuff.</td>', 'Wow, this is just phenomenal work.  The motion capture is really good and the lighting, well, it''s perfect.  The texture on the platform is very important and helps my eye avoid seeing the spinning wheel as floating in midair.  Very good stuff.', '2004-12-05 19:44:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047504, 122288, 12573, '<td valign="top">I wonder what your final score will be because I''m at a loss for how to score your image.  I''m quite fond of the composition.  Still, I''m just not sure about the high contrast, overexposed  nature of the image.  I think I''m going to give you a 6.  There''s just something powerful about the arrangement of the can and the faucet that I like.  Still, the blown out highlights are just too distracting to me to score higher.</td>', 'I wonder what your final score will be because I''m at a loss for how to score your image.  I''m quite fond of the composition.  Still, I''m just not sure about the high contrast, overexposed  nature of the image.  I think I''m going to give you a 6.  There''s just something powerful about the arrangement of the can and the faucet that I like.  Still, the blown out highlights are just too distracting to me to score higher.', '2004-12-05 19:48:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047508, 124707, 12573, '<td valign="top">Low tech indeed.  I''m not sure how much of this remains a true photograph, as it seems to have been converted to something else in post-processing (but forgive me if I''m wrong).  It has a somewhat pop art feel to it, but not enough to warrant consideration as such.  The colors are nice as the muted brown and cyan are very complementary.  It''s something I could imagine seeing being painted in watercolor.  Perhaps I like this more than I thought when I first looked at it.  &lt;shrug&gt;</td>', 'Low tech indeed.  I''m not sure how much of this remains a true photograph, as it seems to have been converted to something else in post-processing (but forgive me if I''m wrong).  It has a somewhat pop art feel to it, but not enough to warrant consideration as such.  The colors are nice as the muted brown and cyan are very complementary.  It''s something I could imagine seeing being painted in watercolor.  Perhaps I like this more than I thought when I first looked at it.  <shrug>', '2004-12-05 19:52:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047540, 124235, 28742, '<td valign="top">Would''ve scroed it higher, but the lighting has a greenish tint.</td>', 'Would''ve scroed it higher, but the lighting has a greenish tint.', '2004-12-05 20:25:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047544, 122388, 28742, '<td valign="top">Oh yeah, tea pots are much more sophisticated nowadays. ;-) Very nice shot - lighting, angle, cropping - good, good, good.</td>', 'Oh yeah, tea pots are much more sophisticated nowadays. ;-) Very nice shot - lighting, angle, cropping - good, good, good.', '2004-12-05 20:27:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047549, 124858, 28742, '<td valign="top">Mmmm Brownies.  Nice job. One of the top ones I''ve seen so far.</td>', 'Mmmm Brownies.  Nice job. One of the top ones I''ve seen so far.', '2004-12-05 20:28:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047553, 123008, 28742, '<td valign="top">Hmmm, this is actually "High Tech" - Low Tech would be the ''ol knife.  Good photo otherwise.</td>', 'Hmmm, this is actually "High Tech" - Low Tech would be the ''ol knife.  Good photo otherwise.', '2004-12-05 20:30:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047557, 122775, 28742, '<td valign="top">At first I wanted to say you should have not cropped or framed so much of the top out, but then I see some ugly industrial buildings back there.  Nice shot.</td>', 'At first I wanted to say you should have not cropped or framed so much of the top out, but then I see some ugly industrial buildings back there.  Nice shot.', '2004-12-05 20:31:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047560, 121834, 28742, '<td valign="top">Yep, I invented that round thing. Never thought it would be of any use. Who knew?  ;-)<br/>I like this shot, but almost think BW would''ve been better, but then you wouldn''t notice the rust. On the other hand - if you think about it, "Low Tech" implies something still in use. This is "Dead Tech"  ;-)</td>', 'Yep, I invented that round thing. Never thought it would be of any use. Who knew?  ;-)I like this shot, but almost think BW would''ve been better, but then you wouldn''t notice the rust. On the other hand - if you think about it, "Low Tech" implies something still in use. This is "Dead Tech"  ;-)', '2004-12-05 20:34:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047565, 124832, 28742, '<td valign="top">That''s more "cutting edge" psychotherapy than low tech dammit!  ;-)</td>', 'That''s more "cutting edge" psychotherapy than low tech dammit!  ;-)', '2004-12-05 20:37:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047567, 124707, 28742, '<td valign="top">Coulda been good, but way over saturated or polarized or whatever it is you did to it. Black &amp; white, different angle or wood big enough to take up all background would''ve made it better for me.</td>', 'Coulda been good, but way over saturated or polarized or whatever it is you did to it. Black & white, different angle or wood big enough to take up all background would''ve made it better for me.', '2004-12-05 20:39:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047569, 124930, 28742, '<td valign="top">...as opposed to the new pitchfork? ;-)  Nice shot.</td>', '...as opposed to the new pitchfork? ;-)  Nice shot.', '2004-12-05 20:40:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047571, 123050, 28742, '<td valign="top">Cool shot. Looks like a unicorn got its horn plucked out. ;-)  Doesn''t scream low tech without an obvious title though.</td>', 'Cool shot. Looks like a unicorn got its horn plucked out. ;-)  Doesn''t scream low tech without an obvious title though.', '2004-12-05 20:42:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047572, 121763, 28742, '<td valign="top">Is this one of those ancient Roman cameras that had tiny hammers &amp; chisels and carved the images in small stone tablets inserted in the back?  ;-)</td>', 'Is this one of those ancient Roman cameras that had tiny hammers & chisels and carved the images in small stone tablets inserted in the back?  ;-)', '2004-12-05 20:44:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047573, 124965, 28742, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot!</td>', 'Beautiful shot!', '2004-12-05 20:44:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047575, 122552, 28742, '<td valign="top">more like "Drifting".  ;-)  Capture some jet skis buzzing around it and it would scream low tech!</td>', 'more like "Drifting".  ;-)  Capture some jet skis buzzing around it and it would scream low tech!', '2004-12-05 20:46:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047580, 124545, 28742, '<td valign="top">Great subject for the challenge. Nice photo in general, but I''d have preferred the background farther back and change lighting to get rid of shadows. Still, one of the better ones seen in this challenge so far.</td>', 'Great subject for the challenge. Nice photo in general, but I''d have preferred the background farther back and change lighting to get rid of shadows. Still, one of the better ones seen in this challenge so far.', '2004-12-05 20:49:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047583, 123235, 28742, '<td valign="top">or "When little Makita was just a boy."  :)  Good shot &amp; this was the first thing that came to my mind when I read the challenge, but I didn''t have a handrill, nor time to put any entries together. This is my top one so far.</td>', 'or "When little Makita was just a boy."  :)  Good shot & this was the first thing that came to my mind when I read the challenge, but I didn''t have a handrill, nor time to put any entries together. This is my top one so far.', '2004-12-05 20:51:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047586, 124888, 28742, '<td valign="top">Oooh. &lt;- That utterance means your photo evoked an immediate reaction. After further study...  Ooooh!  ;-)  I like everything about this shot, but probably the biggest contributing factor is the angle. Great job.</td>', 'Oooh. <- That utterance means your photo evoked an immediate reaction. After further study...  Ooooh!  ;-)  I like everything about this shot, but probably the biggest contributing factor is the angle. Great job.', '2004-12-05 20:54:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047589, 124464, 28742, '<td valign="top">Photo emphasis is more on the creek, the tree and the leafy ground. Took me quite a few cycles of reading the title, staring, reading the title, etc. to even see the wall. Otherwise a nice photo.</td>', 'Photo emphasis is more on the creek, the tree and the leafy ground. Took me quite a few cycles of reading the title, staring, reading the title, etc. to even see the wall. Otherwise a nice photo.', '2004-12-05 20:56:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047590, 124136, 28742, '<td valign="top">This is the first one I''ve seen that compares old and new although not directly. If you could''ve gotten a modern street lamp on the right - it would be a point or 2 higher from me.</td>', 'This is the first one I''ve seen that compares old and new although not directly. If you could''ve gotten a modern street lamp on the right - it would be a point or 2 higher from me.', '2004-12-05 20:58:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047595, 124506, 28742, '<td valign="top">Mmmm...Play Doh....  <br/>A little murky, but good crop and angle.</td>', 'Mmmm...Play Doh....  A little murky, but good crop and angle.', '2004-12-05 21:00:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047606, 124880, 28742, '<td valign="top">I agree with the title! If it wasn''t for that lamp in the background, firemen wouldn''t be able to see the fire hydrant to put out the fire!  ;-)  I''m being facetious, but now that I think about it, maybe you were including the lamp in your title? If that''s the case, I would change my comments to "...and provide a beacon for dogs to relieve themselves."  ;-)  As far as the photo - cropping is good, composition good, challenge appropriateness ok, focus and depth are off though.</td>', 'I agree with the title! If it wasn''t for that lamp in the background, firemen wouldn''t be able to see the fire hydrant to put out the fire!  ;-)  I''m being facetious, but now that I think about it, maybe you were including the lamp in your title? If that''s the case, I would change my comments to "...and provide a beacon for dogs to relieve themselves."  ;-)  As far as the photo - cropping is good, composition good, challenge appropriateness ok, focus and depth are off though.', '2004-12-05 21:06:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047615, 124949, 28742, '<td valign="top">What a coincidence! I am sitting here typing my remarks on an old Underwood! ...oh wait, nevermind - what I mean is I am sitting here in my ''old underwear'' typing my remarks. :-P<br/>Just funnin''.  I like this shot and it is one of the first things I thought of in regards to the challenge topic. Crop might be a little too tight and you could''ve put some paper in it with some old typing on it for more dramatic effect, but overall one of the top pics.</td>', 'What a coincidence! I am sitting here typing my remarks on an old Underwood! ...oh wait, nevermind - what I mean is I am sitting here in my ''old underwear'' typing my remarks. :-PJust funnin''.  I like this shot and it is one of the first things I thought of in regards to the challenge topic. Crop might be a little too tight and you could''ve put some paper in it with some old typing on it for more dramatic effect, but overall one of the top pics.', '2004-12-05 21:10:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047623, 124876, 28742, '<td valign="top">Pretty decent entry, but lighting is a little red and I think it might''ve been more effective if the wrench could''ve been sitting in the bottom of an old toolbox. Good job though.</td>', 'Pretty decent entry, but lighting is a little red and I think it might''ve been more effective if the wrench could''ve been sitting in the bottom of an old toolbox. Good job though.', '2004-12-05 21:13:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047627, 124803, 28742, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot and EXCELLENT title! I like the colors - interestingly, I don''t even think this would be as good in BW.  I think you nailed my top pick so far. Great job.</td>', 'Beautiful shot and EXCELLENT title! I like the colors - interestingly, I don''t even think this would be as good in BW.  I think you nailed my top pick so far. Great job.', '2004-12-05 21:15:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047641, 123656, 28742, '<td valign="top">Score 1 from me.  ;-) Kidding. You should''ve called it "Wagon 10" though.  ;-)<br/>Photographically - it''s got lots of problems (for me). Lighting reflection, angle, focus, tabletop, cropping - all wrong for my taste. Biggest issue though is What the heck am I looking at??  :-) Sorry.  I can think of some funnier titles for you though: "The first atomic bomb is transported to the Enola Gay" or "A truck delivering the worlds largest black olive, passes under the city limits sign."  ...I''ll keep working on it.  ;-)</td>', 'Score 1 from me.  ;-) Kidding. You should''ve called it "Wagon 10" though.  ;-)Photographically - it''s got lots of problems (for me). Lighting reflection, angle, focus, tabletop, cropping - all wrong for my taste. Biggest issue though is What the heck am I looking at??  :-) Sorry.  I can think of some funnier titles for you though: "The first atomic bomb is transported to the Enola Gay" or "A truck delivering the worlds largest black olive, passes under the city limits sign."  ...I''ll keep working on it.  ;-)', '2004-12-05 21:22:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047645, 124946, 28742, '<td valign="top">...or decent task lighting for that matter!  Nice job!</td>', '...or decent task lighting for that matter!  Nice job!', '2004-12-05 21:24:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047649, 124148, 12573, '<td valign="top">Lighting is a bit harsh here (light areas are very bright, while dark areas are very dark).  I think this would have benefitted from a fairly tight crop around the axle nut, leaving out the overexposed hub and keep the OOF (out of focus) rim in view.  This would also help the nut to be less centered in the frame, which is hurting the composition.  The midtones are good and, therefore, this image might be a good candidate for conversion to black and white.  Does not scream "low tech" to me, but what do I know.</td>', 'Lighting is a bit harsh here (light areas are very bright, while dark areas are very dark).  I think this would have benefitted from a fairly tight crop around the axle nut, leaving out the overexposed hub and keep the OOF (out of focus) rim in view.  This would also help the nut to be less centered in the frame, which is hurting the composition.  The midtones are good and, therefore, this image might be a good candidate for conversion to black and white.  Does not scream "low tech" to me, but what do I know.', '2004-12-05 21:25:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047650, 124888, 18933, '<td valign="top">very good lines</td>', 'very good lines', '2004-12-05 21:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047653, 124167, 12573, '<td valign="top">I like the angle.  It lends an artsy feel to an otherwise bland subject.  I think your lighting could have been much improved on this shot.  It''s seems too flat and muddy, as though I were looking at the radio through a dirty fishtank.  This can be a good effect sometimes, but I think it''s not appropriate for this radio.  The gold-ish material on the radio near the top-left is a distraction to me and adds little to the composition.  A tighter crop on just the "TELEFUNKEN" portion, the buttons and the European stations would have been an improvement.  It certainly fits the challenge.  I just would have liked a "cleaner" lighting setup.  Hope that helps.</td>', 'I like the angle.  It lends an artsy feel to an otherwise bland subject.  I think your lighting could have been much improved on this shot.  It''s seems too flat and muddy, as though I were looking at the radio through a dirty fishtank.  This can be a good effect sometimes, but I think it''s not appropriate for this radio.  The gold-ish material on the radio near the top-left is a distraction to me and adds little to the composition.  A tighter crop on just the "TELEFUNKEN" portion, the buttons and the European stations would have been an improvement.  It certainly fits the challenge.  I just would have liked a "cleaner" lighting setup.  Hope that helps.', '2004-12-05 21:26:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047654, 124863, 28742, '<td valign="top">Man, this would''ve been one of my top picks, but the whole image is washed out quite a bit. Would look good with more contrast and saturation...and maybe a little broader angle on the buggy so as to see a little more of the horse and side of the carriage.</td>', 'Man, this would''ve been one of my top picks, but the whole image is washed out quite a bit. Would look good with more contrast and saturation...and maybe a little broader angle on the buggy so as to see a little more of the horse and side of the carriage.', '2004-12-05 21:26:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047657, 124336, 28742, '<td valign="top">Even as children, they never did get along.  ;-)</td>', 'Even as children, they never did get along.  ;-)', '2004-12-05 21:27:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047666, 124968, 28742, '<td valign="top">Good concept, but bad execution. It''s not clear the tape is being used to repair - should''ve shown something damaged and half covered by the tape. Also - the colors are just unpleasant - must be the 70''s paneling. Lastly, too dark and shadowy. Hope this is helpful. :-)</td>', 'Good concept, but bad execution. It''s not clear the tape is being used to repair - should''ve shown something damaged and half covered by the tape. Also - the colors are just unpleasant - must be the 70''s paneling. Lastly, too dark and shadowy. Hope this is helpful. :-)', '2004-12-05 21:30:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047671, 123717, 28742, '<td valign="top">Nice, very nice. Although... I haven''t seen Ronco come up with a device that does what this does!</td>', 'Nice, very nice. Although... I haven''t seen Ronco come up with a device that does what this does!', '2004-12-05 21:31:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1047675, 124153, 28742, '<td valign="top">Very good! Just a few flaws - background could''ve been some more authentic setting and don''t crop part of the iron. Hope this helps.</td>', 'Very good! Just a few flaws - background could''ve been some more authentic setting and don''t crop part of the iron. Hope this helps.', '2004-12-05 21:33:17.000000', NULL, 1),
